#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""dws - director workstreams: the board's current-state ledger.

One row per workstream (an issue, a design and its builds), folded on read
from an append-only event file. Part W1 of the workstream ledger design
(sim/design/board-workstream-ledger.md): the store, the fold, the lock, the
CLI and the instance-id refusal; W2 adds refresh; W3 adds the page and the read of its picks.

  $DIRECTOR_STATE/workstreams.jsonl   append-only events
  $DIRECTOR_STATE/workstreams.lock    one flock around fold, check, append

  dws [--actor A] open <slug> --title T [--owner O] [--stage S] [--repos R..]
                                       [--next N] [--blocked B [--ask ID]] [--link L..]
  dws [--actor A] stage <slug> <to> --from <current>
  dws [--actor A] set <slug> [--owner O] [--next N] [--blocked B [--ask ID]] [--repos R..]
  dws [--actor A] link <slug> [--remove] <link>...
  dws [--actor A] park <slug> --from <current>
  dws refresh [<slug>...]
  dws show [--json]
  dws migrate-blocked-none [--dry-run]
  dws page [--out FILE] [--theme FILE] [--nav FILE] [--desk-url FILE]
  dws picks --file FILE

Links are typed: pr:<owner>/<repo>#<n>, issue:<owner>/<repo>#<n>, bd:<id>
and ask:<id>. refresh (W2) reads the first three; ask ids wait for W5, and an
untyped link is shown but never read. refresh names every link it does not
read on stderr, so nothing is skipped silently.

Waiting: `dws waiting write` is the sweep step that may call gh. It checks each pr: link on a row
that is not parked and writes $DIRECTOR_STATE/waiting-prs.json ({written_at, checked,
approved_not_merged: [{pr, approved_at}]}) for standing-hook, which reads files only. If a PR cannot
be read it writes nothing and exits 1.

Intake: `dws intake --text-file <path|-> [--source S]` records an operator ask in
$DIRECTOR_STATE/asks.jsonl, stamped from the clock under one flock, and prints its id, I-<n>.
The id then travels: relay-log append --ask I-<n> [--kind K], card-ingest parse --intake I-<n>
(desk-snapshot keeps it per card), and an intake:I-<n> link on a row (a typed link, set with
`link` or `open --link`; the name differs from ask:, which is a Desk card id). `dws asks
[--json]` joins them, one row per ask: ask, received_at, card, answered_at, relay, row. A
blank is "none"; the join writes nothing and gives the same bytes for the same files.

K13: `--blocked operator` needs `--ask <card id>`, and refuses unless that card is
open in a Desk snapshot no older than THRESHOLD_HOURS["desk snapshot"] hours. A
session reads the Desk and runs `desk-snapshot write`; without a usable snapshot
dws refuses and says UNREAD, and never takes the id on faith. The card goes on the
row as an ask: link. LF4: when a fresh snapshot shows every ask: card on the row
in a status in CLOSING_STATUSES, `refresh --local` clears the block (set blocked "",
as refresh) and leaves the next action director's. An old closed card never clears
a block that a later, open card holds.

K8: every new event carries "tag", set by dws from the actor and never by a caller:
mirror for refresh (a cited outside fact), judgment for director. proposal is
defined for the reconciler (K11) and refused on append to workstreams.jsonl until it has a
writer (a draft grant in rulings.jsonl carries it). A line
with no tag, or a value that is not a tag, folds as untagged and is never repaired.
show --json counts events by tag per row (since the row was last opened) and ledger-wide
(every event line, including one for a slug with no row, except a set marked migrate); nothing gates on it.

K9: `record ruling|grant|term` appends to rulings.jsonl (the file merge-guard reads for
exclusions; MERGE_GUARD_RULINGS names it, default $DIRECTOR_STATE/rulings.jsonl), under
its own rulings.lock beside it. It never creates the file, refuses the exclusion kind
(the operator's, R-153) and any actor but director, and stores text as given.
`records [--json]` folds the file: replaces is an explicit id pointer; a target is marked
replaced_by, and a pointer to a missing id or another kind is counted, never guessed.

K15: `inherit ROLE [--json]` is the by-role read a successor makes (R-204): the role's standing terms
(a replaced term is marked, not standing), grants in force, pending and expired, and open asks. A
source it cannot read is UNREAD and its section is none, never an empty list. Read only.

K14: `ring SEAT --idle-minutes N --mail N` records a ring in rings.jsonl (Q6: 10 minutes idle with
mail, at most 3 rings per seat per hour, then it refuses and the seat is reported stuck);
`ring-note SEAT first-turn|ack|blocker [--text T]` follows it; `rings [--json]` reads per seat.

K10: `grant-card <id> [--out FILE]` renders the Desk card that shows a draft grant's bounds, in
card-ingest's format. `grant-confirm <id> --card C --quote WORDS` records the grant as confirmed
(replacing the draft, which is never edited) only when the fresh Desk snapshot lists C as answered;
the quote is the session's claim of the operator's words.

K18: `digest` renders the operator digest and the close-or-kill list on demand, from the reconciler and the
queue, to stdout and $DIRECTOR_STATE/digest.md; nothing runs it on a clock. Its interrupt list is the Q1
default list (DIGEST_INTERRUPTS), for the operator to edit.

K12: `queue [--json]` is the operator's queue: the open Desk cards joined to ledger rows by their ask: links.
A card whose linked PRs are all observed draft, merged or closed is hidden until director closes it; any other
open card is shown, and a card no row links is "unclassified, shown". The checks that need card fields the
snapshot lacks (kind, text, source) are listed as not run. Read only. While the ledger has a torn line nothing is
hidden; dws never repairs one, so the operator clears it by correcting or removing that line of workstreams.jsonl
(`dws show` and `dws queue` print the unreadable-line count), and hiding resumes on the next run.

K19: `board-state` rewrites only the text between `<!-- state:begin -->` and `<!-- state:end -->` in
$DIRECTOR_STATE/board.md from the ledger and the Desk snapshot (the block goes first when there are no
markers; a malformed pair is refused and nothing is written; dws never creates board.md). `board-check
[--json]` lists the `ask:<id>` and `ws:<slug>` ids in the prose that resolve to no record, exits 0, and
says "not checked" for an id whose store is UNREAD. The block takes its line ending from the board's first
line (CRLF if that line ends in one, else LF), so a board already mixed gets one ending in the block and keeps
its other lines as they are: the rule is cheap to state and never rewrites authored text; it is not a claim
that a mixed board is well formed.

K11: `reconcile [--json] [--out FILE]` reads the Desk snapshot, the ledger, rulings.jsonl,
rings.jsonl and the PR state the ledger observed, and writes proposals (tag proposal) to
$DIRECTOR_STATE/reconcile-proposals.json. It appends no record to any store. Each source
prints its last-read time or UNREAD, the queue count reads "at least n" while any source is
UNREAD, and a check with no readable source (recommendation sell-by, an ask unacked past
its window, a harvest due) is listed as not run, never counted as zero.

D1: `decision add --from FILE` parses one seat-decision@1 block (sim/design/seat-decisions.md,
section 3) and appends a decision event, state decided-by-seat, to workstreams.jsonl under the same
lock as the rows. `decision actual|confirm|override|rework` record the actual figure and the three
moves (decided-by-seat to confirmed or overridden, overridden to reworked); confirm and override keep
the operator's words as given. A skip is no command, and no move happens on a clock. `decisions
[--json] [--unconfirmed] [--daily --trial-start DATE]` reads them and writes nothing. The wait edges,
the window and the affected list are D2.

D2: `set --waits decision:<id>` and `--unwait` keep a row's wait edges to decisions in their own field
(waits, never links), as `wait` events; `link` refuses a decision: string. A decision takes at most three
dependents (rows with an edge that are not parked) and no new one more than 120 hours after its add, and
the same checks run when `stage` moves a row out of parked. `decisions` orders the unconfirmed with a full
window first and carries the affected rows; `decision override` prints them and `rework` refuses while one
is open. `decision paths|pick|withdraw` record two paths at once (section 8). `merge-hold REPO#N` is the
read merge-guard makes: it holds a PR whose row waits on a decision that is not confirmed.

A blocked value of "none" (any case) means not blocked: `open` and `set` store it as empty, so
every reader sees the same thing. `migrate-blocked-none` clears the "none" values stored before
that, one set event per row marked migrate, which does not move the row's last moved time; it
changes nothing but those rows, and a second run finds none. --dry-run names the rows and
writes nothing.

The actor is a claim, not an identity: the writer table is an allowlist over
--actor, and a caller that passes --actor refresh is believed (section 6).
"""
import argparse, datetime, fcntl, hashlib, html as htmlmod, json, os, re, subprocess, sys, tempfile, time, unicodedata

HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
STATE = os.environ.get("DIRECTOR_STATE") or f"{HOME}/.director/state"
LEDGER = os.path.join(STATE, "workstreams.jsonl")
LOCK = os.path.join(STATE, "workstreams.lock")
LOCK_TIMEOUT = 5.0
SNAPSHOT = os.path.join(STATE, "desk-snapshot.json")

# K13: hours a Desk snapshot may age before dws reads it as UNREAD (finding-
# director-glst; the table of the automation boundary, ADR-007). A diagnostic
# bound, not a gate on anything else. The operator changes it here.
THRESHOLD_HOURS = {"desk snapshot": 24}

# LF4 (ledger-fill.md section 3, operator ruling 1 of 2026-10-19): a Desk card in one of
# these statuses has closed, so refresh clears the operator block on a row that links it.
# A wrong entry clears a block early, so the table is the operator's to edit, here.
CLOSING_STATUSES = ("closed", "resolved", "withdrawn", "superseded", "relayed")

# Section 3. The order is the sort order; parked sorts last.
STAGES = ["idea", "defined", "designed", "building", "in review", "merged",
          "released", "deployed", "accepted", "parked"]

# Section 6, the writer table. refresh may append observe events and the two
# factual stage moves of section 5; anything not listed may append nothing.
REFRESH_MOVES = {("building", "in review"), ("in review", "merged")}
ACTORS = {"director", "refresh"}

# K8: every new event carries a tag that dws sets itself from the actor; no
# caller passes one. mirror is a cited outside fact (refresh), judgment is
# director's own call. proposal (needs a confirm) is defined for K11, which has
# no writer yet, so dws refuses to append it. A line with no tag, or with a
# value that is not one of these, folds as "untagged" and is never repaired.
TAGS = ("mirror", "proposal", "judgment")
APPENDABLE_TAGS = ("mirror", "judgment")
ACTOR_TAG = {"refresh": "mirror", "director": "judgment"}
UNTAGGED = "untagged"

SLUG = re.compile(r"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]*$")
# Section 2: a token like g9-9 anywhere in a value's match key is an instance
# id. Instance ids change at every respawn; a role does not.
INSTANCE_ID = re.compile(r"(^|[^a-z0-9])(g[0-9]+ ?- ?[0-9]+)")


class Refused(Exception):
    pass


def now():
    """The clock, as the ledger writes it. DWS_NOW overrides it only when
    DWS_TEST_CLOCK=1 is also set (the verify scripts, which need a fixed now
    on either side of their fixtures), so a stray DWS_NOW cannot pin the
    ledger's timestamps."""
    fixed = os.environ.get("DWS_NOW") if os.environ.get("DWS_TEST_CLOCK") == "1" else None
    if fixed:
        return fixed
    return datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def stored_form(value):
    """What dws writes (two-form rule, re-ruled 2026-10-02, director#195):
    NFKC; every whitespace run, Cc whitespace included, to one space, trimmed;
    the remaining Cc stripped. Nothing else is removed or mapped, so marks,
    selectors, joiners and dashes in real text are stored as typed."""
    v = unicodedata.normalize("NFKC", value)
    v = re.sub(r"\s+", " ", v).strip()
    return "".join(ch for ch in v if unicodedata.category(ch) != "Cc")


def match_keys(stored):
    """The keys the instance-id refusal matches on, computed from the stored
    form and never stored. U+00AD is taken both ways, mapped to '-' and
    removed, since either reading can be the one that hides an id; then
    NFKD, so a mark composed onto a letter comes apart; Cf, Mn, Mc and Me
    stripped; Pd and U+2212 to '-'; whitespace runs collapsed again, since a
    stripped character between two spaces leaves two; lower case."""
    keys = []
    for shy in ("-", ""):
        v = unicodedata.normalize("NFKD", stored.replace("\u00ad", shy))
        v = "".join(ch for ch in v if unicodedata.category(ch) not in ("Cf", "Mn", "Mc", "Me"))
        v = "".join("-" if unicodedata.category(ch) == "Pd" or ch == "\u2212" else ch for ch in v)
        keys.append(re.sub(r"\s+", " ", v).lower())
    return keys


def checked(field, value):
    """The stored form, or Refused when either match key carries an instance id."""
    stored = stored_form(value)
    for key in match_keys(stored):
        m = INSTANCE_ID.search(key)
        if m:
            raise Refused(f"{field} {value!r} carries instance id {m.group(2)!r}; "
                          "name the seat or role, never an instance id (they change at "
                          "every respawn). Reword the value if the token is not an id.")
    return stored


def parse_time(ts):
    return datetime.datetime.strptime(ts, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ").replace(tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)


def operator_blocked(value):
    """True when a blocked value is the operator, in any form dws stores alike."""
    return stored_form(value).lower() == "operator"


def desk_card_open(card_id):
    """K13: the card id must be open in a fresh Desk snapshot. Returns the
    snapshot's age text, or raises Refused. Without a usable snapshot it
    refuses and says UNREAD; it never takes the id on faith."""
    hint = "a session must read the Desk and run desk-snapshot write"
    try:
        with open(SNAPSHOT, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            snap = json.load(f)
        read_at = parse_time(snap["read_at"])
        open_ids = snap["open"]
        if not isinstance(open_ids, list) or not all(isinstance(i, str) for i in open_ids):
            raise ValueError("open is not a list of ids")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        raise Refused(f"the Desk snapshot is UNREAD: {SNAPSHOT} does not exist; {hint}")
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError) as err:
        raise Refused(f"the Desk snapshot is UNREAD: {SNAPSHOT} cannot be read ({type(err).__name__}); {hint}")
    age = parse_time(now()) - read_at
    hours = age.total_seconds() / 3600
    limit = THRESHOLD_HOURS["desk snapshot"]
    if hours < 0:
        raise Refused(f"the Desk snapshot is UNREAD: it was read at {snap['read_at']}, which is in the future; {hint}")
    if hours > limit:
        raise Refused(f"the Desk snapshot is UNREAD: it was read {int(hours)}h ago and the limit is {limit}h; {hint}")
    if card_id not in open_ids:
        raise Refused(f"card {card_id!r} is not open in the Desk snapshot read at {snap['read_at']}; "
                      "name an open card, or open one first")
    return f"card {card_id} is open in the Desk snapshot read {int(hours)}h ago ({snap['read_at']})"


def blocked_stored(field, stored):
    """A blocked value of none, in any case, is not blocked: it is stored as empty."""
    return "" if field == "blocked" and stored.lower() == "none" else stored


def blocked_on_operator(blocked, ask):
    """Applies K13 to one write. Returns the ask link to add, or None."""
    if ask is not None and (blocked is None or not operator_blocked(blocked)):
        raise Refused("--ask goes with --blocked operator only")
    if blocked is None or not operator_blocked(blocked):
        return None
    if ask is None:
        raise Refused("--blocked operator needs --ask <card id>, an open card on the Desk (K13)")
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]*", ask):
        raise Refused(f"--ask {ask!r} is not a card id")
    print(f"dws: {desk_card_open(ask)}")
    return f"ask:{ask}"


def fold(path=LEDGER, tally=None, decisions=None):
    """Rows by slug, and how many lines could not be read. A torn line is
    skipped and counted, never repaired. A tally dict, when given, counts every
    event line by tag, whatever became of it: a line for a slug with no row and
    a re-open that resets a row are both in it (K8). A decisions dict, when
    given, takes the decision events (D1); they never touch a row."""
    rows, torn = {}, 0
    try:
        f = open(path, "rb")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return rows, 0
    with f:
        for line in f:
            if not line.strip():
                continue
            try:
                e = json.loads(line.decode("utf-8"))
            except ValueError:
                torn += 1
                continue
            if not isinstance(e, dict):
                torn += 1
                continue
            # The ledger-wide count reads as how often director judged, so a set that
            # migrate-blocked-none wrote is left out of it, as it is out of the row's own.
            if tally is not None and not (e.get("event") == "set" and e.get("migrate")):
                name = tag_name(e)
                tally[name] = tally.get(name, 0) + 1
            if e.get("event") == "decision":
                if decisions is not None:
                    apply_decision(decisions, e)
                continue
            apply(rows, e)
    return rows, torn


def tag_name(e):
    """A line with no tag, or with a value that is not a tag, is untagged and is
    never read as judgment."""
    t = e.get("tag")
    return t if isinstance(t, str) and t in TAGS else UNTAGGED


def count_tag(row, e):
    """K8: the events applied to the row since it was last opened, by tag."""
    name = tag_name(e)
    row["tags"][name] = row["tags"].get(name, 0) + 1


def apply(rows, e):
    slug, ev, ts = e.get("ws"), e.get("event"), e.get("ts", "")
    if ev == "open":
        rows[slug] = {
            "slug": slug, "title": e.get("title", ""), "repos": e.get("repos", []),
            "owner": e.get("owner", ""), "stage": e.get("stage", "idea"),
            "last_moved": ts, "next": e.get("next", ""), "blocked": e.get("blocked", ""),
            "links": list(e.get("links", [])), "opened": ts,
            "hints": [], "observed": {}, "facts": [], "tags": {}, "consumed": [], "waits": [],
        }
        count_tag(rows[slug], e)
        return
    r = rows.get(slug)
    if r is None:
        return
    # A set that migrate-blocked-none wrote is housekeeping: it is not an event of the row's own
    # history, so it joins neither the tag tally nor (below) last moved.
    if not (ev == "set" and e.get("migrate")):
        count_tag(r, e)
    if ev in ("stage", "park"):
        r["stage"] = e.get("to", "parked" if ev == "park" else r["stage"])
        r["last_moved"] = max(r["last_moved"], ts)
        if e.get("actor") == "refresh" and e.get("fact"):
            r["facts"].append(e["fact"])
    elif ev == "set":
        for k in ("owner", "next", "blocked", "repos"):
            if k in e:
                r[k] = e[k]
        # R-197: an authored update counts as movement. It never moves the clock back. A set that
        # migrate-blocked-none wrote is housekeeping, not an update, and moves nothing.
        if not e.get("migrate"):
            r["last_moved"] = max(r["last_moved"], ts)
    elif ev == "link":
        for link in e.get("add", []):
            if link not in r["links"]:
                r["links"].append(link)
        r["links"] = [x for x in r["links"] if x not in e.get("remove", [])]
    elif ev == "wait":
        # D2: a decision edge, apart from links. The check ran on write; a stored line is applied as it stands.
        for did in e.get("add", []):
            if did not in r["waits"]:
                r["waits"].append(did)
        r["waits"] = [x for x in r["waits"] if x not in e.get("remove", [])]
        r["last_moved"] = max(r["last_moved"], ts)
    elif ev == "observe":
        # A src names the fact an event consumed (ledger fill, section 6); the fill
        # skips any src already here, so replaying a source writes nothing.
        src = e.get("src")
        if isinstance(src, str) and src not in r["consumed"]:
            r["consumed"] = sorted(r["consumed"] + [src])
        # refresh records what it saw; a linked artifact that moved moves the
        # row's last-moved time (section 5). A row-level observe (no link)
        # carries the hints from that refresh.
        if e.get("moved_at"):
            r["last_moved"] = max(r["last_moved"], e["moved_at"])
        if e.get("link"):
            r["observed"][e["link"]] = {"seen": e.get("seen", {}), "checked_at": e.get("checked_at", ts)}
        elif "hints" in e:
            r["hints"] = list(e["hints"])


def sorted_rows(rows):
    return sorted(rows.values(), key=lambda r: (STAGES.index(r["stage"]) if r["stage"] in STAGES else len(STAGES), r["last_moved"], r["slug"]))


class Locked:
    """One exclusive flock around fold, check and append. A holder that does
    not let go within LOCK_TIMEOUT is a loud failure, not a wait forever."""

    def __init__(self, path=None):
        self.path = path

    def __enter__(self):
        if self.path is None:
            os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
        lock = self.path or LOCK
        self.f = open(lock, "a")
        deadline = time.monotonic() + LOCK_TIMEOUT
        while True:
            try:
                fcntl.flock(self.f, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
                return self
            except BlockingIOError:
                if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
                    self.f.close()
                    raise Refused(f"ledger lock {lock} held for more than {LOCK_TIMEOUT:.0f}s; nothing written")
                time.sleep(0.05)

    def __exit__(self, *exc):
        fcntl.flock(self.f, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
        self.f.close()


def append(event, path=None):
    """Append one whole line. A torn last line is left as it is; the new event
    starts on its own line so it is not glued to the torn one."""
    path = path or LEDGER
    line = json.dumps(event, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":")) + "\n"
    with open(path, "ab") as f:
        if f.tell() > 0:
            with open(path, "rb") as r:
                r.seek(-1, os.SEEK_END)
                if r.read(1) != b"\n":
                    line = "\n" + line
        f.write(line.encode("utf-8"))
        f.flush()
        os.fsync(f.fileno())


def allowed(actor, event):
    if actor not in ACTORS:
        raise Refused(f"actor {actor!r} may append nothing; writers are {sorted(ACTORS)} (section 6)")
    if actor == "refresh":
        ev = event["event"]
        if ev in ("observe", "refresh-run"):
            return
        if ev == "stage" and (event.get("from"), event.get("to")) in REFRESH_MOVES:
            return
        # LF4: one set, of blocked to empty and no other field, carrying the Desk read it came
        # from. The fill checks that the row is blocked on the operator and that every ask:
        # card it links is in a closing status.
        if (ev == "set" and {k for k in ("owner", "next", "blocked", "repos") if k in event} == {"blocked"}
                and event["blocked"] == "" and str(event.get("src", "")).startswith("desk:")):
            return
        raise Refused("refresh may append observe events, its run record, the two factual stage moves "
                      "(building to in review, in review to merged) and the fill's clear of an operator block "
                      "whose Desk card closed (LF4) only; director makes every other move")


def check_tag(tag):
    if tag not in TAGS:
        raise Refused(f"tag {tag!r} is not one of {', '.join(TAGS)}")
    if tag not in APPENDABLE_TAGS:
        raise Refused(f"the {tag} tag is defined and not appended yet; K11 gives it a writer")


def stamp(actor, event):
    """The event as it is written: ts, actor and the tag dws sets from the
    actor, then the fields. A tag the caller put in the event is dropped."""
    fields = {k: v for k, v in event.items() if k != "tag"}
    allowed(actor, fields)
    tag = ACTOR_TAG[actor]
    check_tag(tag)
    return {"ts": now(), "actor": actor, "tag": tag, **fields}


def write(actor, event, check):
    """Fold, check, append under the lock. check(rows) raises Refused."""
    event = stamp(actor, event)
    with Locked():
        rows, _ = fold()
        check(rows)
        append(event)
    rerender()


def write_many(actor, plan, run_record=None):
    """Fold, then let plan(rows) return the events to append, all under one
    lock, so the stage each move is checked against is the current one.
    run_record, when given, is called with the events and returns the run's
    own record, appended last under the same lock (the ops dashboard's check
    that the refresh ran). It is not among the events returned, so a run that
    changed nothing still prints and re-renders nothing."""
    with Locked():
        rows, _ = fold()
        events = [stamp(actor, e) for e in plan(rows)]
        for e in events:
            append(e)
        # A fill launched by the board renderer (DWS_NO_RERENDER=1) is not a refresh run by director: it
        # would move the ledger file's mtime on every render and so hide the page's "ledger Nm" age.
        if run_record is not None and not os.environ.get("DWS_NO_RERENDER"):
            append(stamp(actor, run_record(events)))
    if events:
        rerender()
    return events


def write_plan(actor, plan):
    """Fold rows and decisions together, let plan(rows, decisions) return the events or raise Refused,
    and append them under one lock, so every check sees the state the write lands on (D2)."""
    with Locked():
        decisions = {}
        rows, _ = fold(decisions=decisions)
        events = [stamp(actor, e) for e in plan(rows, decisions)]
        for e in events:
            append(e)
    if events:
        rerender()
    return events


def rerender():
    """After a write, re-render the page when board.html exists (opt-in by
    existence, the rule the renderer already follows). board-html launches the
    fill with DWS_NO_RERENDER=1, so a render never re-renders itself."""
    if os.environ.get("DWS_NO_RERENDER") or not os.path.exists(os.path.join(STATE, "board.html")):
        return
    renderer = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "board-html")
    try:
        subprocess.run([renderer], check=True, capture_output=True, timeout=30)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as err:
        print(f"dws: written; board-html re-render failed: {err}", file=sys.stderr)


def need(rows, slug):
    if slug not in rows:
        raise Refused(f"no workstream {slug!r}; open it first")
    return rows[slug]


def stage_name(s):
    if s not in STAGES:
        raise Refused(f"unknown stage {s!r}; stages are: {', '.join(STAGES)}")
    return s


def cmd_open(a):
    if not SLUG.match(a.slug):
        raise Refused(f"slug {a.slug!r} must be lower case letters, digits, '.', '_' or '-'")
    ev = {"event": "open", "ws": a.slug, "title": a.title, "stage": stage_name(a.stage)}
    for field in ("owner", "next", "blocked"):
        v = getattr(a, field)
        if v is not None:
            ev[field] = blocked_stored(field, checked(field, v))
    if a.repos:
        ev["repos"] = a.repos
    ask_link = blocked_on_operator(a.blocked, a.ask)
    if ask_link:
        ev["blocked"] = "operator"
    for link in a.link or []:
        decision_link_refused(link)
        if link.startswith("intake:"):
            typed_link(link)
    if a.link or ask_link:
        ev["links"] = list(a.link or []) + ([ask_link] if ask_link and ask_link not in (a.link or []) else [])

    def check(rows):
        if a.slug in rows:
            raise Refused(f"workstream {a.slug!r} is already open; use set, stage or link")
    write(a.actor, ev, check)


def move(a, event, to):
    ev = {"event": event, "ws": a.slug, "from": stage_name(a.from_), "to": stage_name(to)}

    def plan(rows, decisions):
        r = need(rows, a.slug)
        cur = r["stage"]
        if cur != a.from_:
            raise Refused(f"stale move: {a.slug!r} is in {cur!r}, not {a.from_!r}; re-read and retry")
        if cur == "parked" and ev["to"] != "parked":
            # D2 section 5: out of parked, the row is a dependent again, so the window applies to
            # every decision it still waits on that has not been answered.
            t_now = parse_time(now())
            for did in r.get("waits", []):
                if decisions.get(did, {}).get("state") in DECISION_OPEN:
                    window_check(rows, decisions, did, a.slug, t_now)
        return [ev]
    write_plan(a.actor, plan)


def cmd_stage(a):
    move(a, "stage", a.to)


def cmd_park(a):
    move(a, "park", "parked")


def wait_ids(values, flag):
    """The decision ids of --waits or --unwait values, in order; Refused on any other kind."""
    ids = []
    for v in values or []:
        if not v.startswith("decision:") or len(v) == len("decision:"):
            raise Refused(f"{flag} takes decision:<id>" + (" or ask:<card id>" if flag == "--waits" else "") + f", not {v!r}")
        ids.append(stored_form(v[len("decision:"):]))
    return ids


def cmd_set(a):
    ev = {"event": "set", "ws": a.slug}
    for field in ("owner", "next", "blocked"):
        v = getattr(a, field)
        if v is not None:
            ev[field] = blocked_stored(field, checked(field, v))
    if a.repos is not None:
        ev["repos"] = a.repos
    # --waits ask:<card> keeps K13 and stays a link; --waits decision:<id> is a wait edge.
    asks = [v for v in a.waits or [] if v.startswith("ask:")]
    waits = wait_ids([v for v in a.waits or [] if not v.startswith("ask:")], "--waits")
    unwaits = wait_ids(a.unwait, "--unwait")
    ask_links = []
    ask_link = blocked_on_operator(a.blocked, a.ask)
    if ask_link:
        ev["blocked"] = "operator"
        ask_links.append(ask_link)
    for v in asks:
        card = v[len("ask:"):]
        if not card or not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]*", card):
            raise Refused(f"--waits {v!r} is not ask:<card id>")
        print(f"dws: {desk_card_open(card)}")
        if v not in ask_links:
            ask_links.append(v)
    if len(ev) == 2 and not ask_links and not waits and not unwaits:
        raise Refused("set needs at least one of --owner, --next, --blocked, --repos, --waits, --unwait")

    def plan(rows, decisions):
        r = need(rows, a.slug)
        events = [ev] if len(ev) > 2 or ask_link else []
        links = [l for l in ask_links if l not in r["links"]]
        if links:
            events.append({"event": "link", "ws": a.slug, "add": links})
        t_now = parse_time(now())
        for did in waits:
            if did in r["waits"]:
                continue
            window_check(rows, decisions, did, a.slug, t_now)
            events.append({"event": "wait", "ws": a.slug, "add": [did]})
        for did in unwaits:
            if did not in r["waits"]:
                raise Refused(f"{a.slug!r} has no edge to decision {did!r}; nothing to drop")
            if decisions.get(did, {}).get("state") in DECISION_OPEN:
                raise Refused(f"decision {did!r} is {decisions[did]['state']!r}: an edge cannot be dropped before a "
                              "confirm, so a PR cannot stop waiting by losing its edge; park the row instead")
            events.append({"event": "wait", "ws": a.slug, "remove": [did]})
        return events
    write_plan(a.actor, plan)


RELAY_LINK = re.compile(r"^relay:R-[0-9]+$")
MSG_LINK = re.compile(r"^msg:[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]*$")
INTAKE_ID = re.compile(r"^I-[0-9]+$")
INTAKE_LINK = re.compile(r"^intake:I-[0-9]+$")


def typed_link(link):
    """relay: and msg: links are typed (ledger fill): a malformed one is refused, so a
    typo cannot sit on a row looking like a join key. Other links are untouched."""
    if link.startswith("relay:") and not RELAY_LINK.match(link):
        raise Refused(f"link {link!r} is not relay:R-<n>")
    if link.startswith("msg:") and not MSG_LINK.match(link):
        raise Refused(f"link {link!r} is not msg:<message id>")
    if link.startswith("intake:") and not INTAKE_LINK.match(link):
        raise Refused(f"link {link!r} is not intake:I-<n>")
    return link


def decision_link_refused(link):
    if link.startswith("decision:"):
        raise Refused(f"link {link!r}: a decision edge is set with dws set --waits, which holds it to the window")


def cmd_link(a):
    for link in a.links:
        typed_link(link)
        if not a.remove:
            decision_link_refused(link)
    ev = {"event": "link", "ws": a.slug, ("remove" if a.remove else "add"): a.links}
    write(a.actor, ev, lambda rows: need(rows, a.slug))


# The links refresh reads. A bd id must start with a letter or digit, so it can
# never reach bd as an option. ask: is typed but not read until W5; any other
# link is untyped. refresh names every link it does not read.
LINK = re.compile(r"^(pr|issue):([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+)#([0-9]+)$|^(bd):([A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*)$")
ASK = re.compile(r"^ask:\S+$")


def refresh_skip():
    return float(os.environ.get("DWS_REFRESH_SKIP_SECONDS", "600"))


def parse_ts(ts):
    try:
        return datetime.datetime.strptime(ts, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ").replace(tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return None


def run_json(cmd):
    out = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
    if out.returncode != 0:
        raise RuntimeError((out.stderr or out.stdout).strip() or f"exit {out.returncode}")
    return out.stdout


def pr_state(d):
    if d.get("mergedAt") or d.get("state") == "MERGED":
        return "merged"
    if d.get("state") == "CLOSED":
        return "closed"
    return "draft" if d.get("isDraft") else "ready"


def release_containing(repo, commit):
    """The latest stable release tag of repo (GitHub's releases/latest, which
    leaves out drafts and pre-releases) when its history contains commit, or
    None. A repo with no stable release answers 404, which is None, not a
    failure. A hint only: refresh never moves a row to released (section 5)."""
    if not commit:
        return None
    try:
        tag = run_json(["gh", "api", f"repos/{repo}/releases/latest", "--jq", ".tag_name"]).strip()
    except RuntimeError as err:
        if "HTTP 404" in str(err):
            return None
        raise
    if not tag:
        return None
    status = run_json(["gh", "api", f"repos/{repo}/compare/{commit}...{tag}", "--jq", ".status"]).strip()
    return tag if status in ("ahead", "identical") else None


def pr_moved_at(d):
    """When the PR last moved in the sense of the section 5 table: its latest
    commit, review or merge. A comment changes updatedAt and is not a move. A
    ready event carries no time here; refresh dates it by the state change."""
    times = [c.get("committedDate") for c in d.get("commits") or []]
    times += [r.get("submittedAt") for r in d.get("reviews") or []]
    times.append(d.get("mergedAt"))
    times = [t for t in times if t]
    return max(times) if times else None


def fetch(link, last_seen=None):
    """What the source says now: (seen, moved_at). Reads only."""
    m = LINK.match(link)
    kind = m.group(1) or m.group(4)
    if kind == "pr":
        repo, num = m.group(2), m.group(3)
        d = json.loads(run_json(["gh", "pr", "view", num, "-R", repo, "--json",
                                 "state,isDraft,reviewDecision,updatedAt,mergedAt,mergeCommit,commits,reviews"]))
        seen = {"kind": "pr", "state": pr_state(d)}
        moved = pr_moved_at(d)
        if last_seen and last_seen.get("state") and last_seen["state"] != seen["state"]:
            moved = max(filter(None, [moved, now()]))  # ready, merge or close seen now
        if seen["state"] == "merged":
            # A hint only (section 5): a release check that fails is a hint
            # too, and never costs the PR its observation or its move.
            commit = (d.get("mergeCommit") or {}).get("oid")
            try:
                tag = release_containing(repo, commit)
            except (RuntimeError, ValueError, OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, KeyError) as err:
                seen["release_error"] = str(err).splitlines()[0][:200] if str(err) else type(err).__name__
            else:
                if tag:
                    seen["release"] = tag
        return seen, moved
    if kind == "issue":
        repo, num = m.group(2), m.group(3)
        d = json.loads(run_json(["gh", "issue", "view", num, "-R", repo, "--json", "state,updatedAt"]))
        return {"kind": "issue", "state": d.get("state", "").lower()}, d.get("updatedAt")
    d = json.loads(run_json(["bd", "show", m.group(5), "--json"]))
    d = d[0] if isinstance(d, list) and d else d
    moved = d.get("updated_at")
    if moved and not moved.endswith("Z"):
        t = datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(moved)
        moved = t.astimezone(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")
    return {"kind": "bd", "state": d.get("status", "")}, moved


def decide(row, seen_by_link):
    """The factual moves and the hints for one row (section 5). A PR closed
    unmerged is left out of the agreement and shown. A fact is the set of the
    row's PRs with their states, never a time; a fact already recorded on an
    earlier refresh move is never applied again, so a revert holds until a PR
    reaches a state not acted on before."""
    prs = sorted((link, s["state"]) for link, s in seen_by_link.items() if s.get("kind") == "pr")
    hints = [f"PR {link[3:]} closed unmerged" for link, st in prs if st == "closed"]
    active = [(link, st) for link, st in prs if st != "closed"]
    for link, s in seen_by_link.items():
        if s.get("release"):
            hints.append(f"release {s['release']} contains {link[3:]}; moving to released is director's call")
        if s.get("release_error"):
            hints.append(f"release check for {link[3:]} failed ({s['release_error']}); no release hint")
    if not active:
        return [], hints
    fact = ", ".join(f"{link[3:]} {st}" for link, st in prs)
    states = {st for _, st in active}
    moves, stage = [], row["stage"]
    if fact not in row["facts"]:
        if stage == "building" and states <= {"ready", "merged"}:
            moves.append(("building", "in review"))
            stage = "in review"
        if stage == "in review" and states == {"merged"}:
            moves.append(("in review", "merged"))
            stage = "merged"
    if not moves and stage in ("building", "in review") and len(states) > 1:
        hints.append("linked PRs disagree (" + ", ".join(f"{link[3:]} {st}" for link, st in active) + "); stage left as is")
    return [{"event": "stage", "ws": row["slug"], "from": f, "to": t, "fact": fact} for f, t in moves], hints


def cmd_refresh(a):
    if a.local:
        return cmd_refresh_local(a)
    """Read each row's linked sources and record what they say (W2). Network
    reads happen outside the lock; the moves are decided under it, against
    the stage as it is then. Appends as actor refresh whatever --actor says."""
    rows, _ = fold()
    slugs = a.slugs or [r["slug"] for r in sorted_rows(rows)]
    for slug in slugs:
        need(rows, slug)
    t_now = parse_ts(now())
    observed, warnings = {}, []
    for slug in slugs:
        row = rows[slug]
        for link in row["links"]:
            if not LINK.match(link):
                if link.startswith("relay:"):
                    why = "relay entries are read by refresh --local"
                elif link.startswith("msg:"):
                    why = "ask ledger rows are read in W5"
                else:
                    why = "Desk cards are read by refresh --local" if ASK.match(link) else "untyped; use pr:, issue: or bd:<id>"
                warnings.append(f"{slug}: {link} not read ({why})")
                continue
            last = row["observed"].get(link)
            checked = parse_ts(last["checked_at"]) if last else None
            if checked and (t_now - checked).total_seconds() < refresh_skip():
                continue
            try:
                seen, moved = fetch(link, last["seen"] if last else None)
            except (RuntimeError, ValueError, OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, KeyError) as err:
                warnings.append(f"{slug}: {link} unreadable: {err}")
                continue
            observed[(slug, link)] = (seen, moved)

    def plan(current):
        events = []
        for slug in slugs:
            row = current.get(slug)
            if row is None:
                continue
            seen_by_link = {link: v["seen"] for link, v in row["observed"].items() if link in row["links"]}
            for (s, link), (seen, moved) in observed.items():
                if s != slug:
                    continue
                ev = {"event": "observe", "ws": slug, "link": link, "seen": seen, "checked_at": now()}
                if moved:
                    # A source time ahead of now (a skewed or forged commit
                    # date) would sort as freshest forever; clamp it.
                    ev["moved_at"] = min(moved, now())
                events.append(ev)
                seen_by_link[link] = seen
            moves, hints = decide(row, seen_by_link)
            events.extend(moves)
            if hints != row["hints"]:
                events.append({"event": "observe", "ws": slug, "hints": hints, "checked_at": now()})
        return events

    events = write_many("refresh", plan, lambda evs: {"event": "refresh-run", "at": now(), "rows": len(slugs),
                                                      "links": len(observed), "warnings": len(warnings)})
    for e in events:
        if e["event"] == "stage":
            print(f"{e['ws']}: {e['from']} -> {e['to']} ({e['fact']})")
        elif "hints" in e:
            for h in e["hints"]:
                print(f"{e['ws']}: hint: {h}")
    for w in warnings:
        print(f"dws refresh: {w}", file=sys.stderr)



# ---- ledger fill (sim/design/ledger-fill.md, issue #321) ---------------------------------------
# refresh --local reads only local records: the relay log, the Desk snapshot. An event is tied
# to a row by an id its writer recorded (relay-log --ws, a relay:R-<n> link, an ask:<card>
# link) and never by reading message text (R-186, authority-never-in-content). Each event it
# appends carries src, the fact it consumed; the fold keeps that set per row and the fill skips
# any src already there, so replaying the same sources writes nothing. Its events are observe,
# plus the LF4 clear of an operator block whose linked card closed.
RELAY_LOCK_TIMEOUT = 5.0
RELAY_HEAD = re.compile(r"^## R-([0-9]+) \((\d{4}-\d\d-\d\dT\d\d:\d\d:\d\dZ)\) -> (.+)$")
RELAY_OUTCOME = re.compile(r"^### R-([0-9]+) outcome \((\d{4}-\d\d-\d\dT\d\d:\d\d:\d\dZ)\)$")
WS_FIELD = re.compile(r"^\*\*Workstream:\*\* (.+)$")
INTAKE_FIELD = re.compile(r"^\*\*Intake:\*\* (I-[0-9]+)$")


def relay_path():
    """The relay log, found as relay-log finds it: $RELAY_LOG, else the checkout's
    sim/notes/relay-log.md when this script runs through a symlink into a checkout."""
    env = os.environ.get("RELAY_LOG")
    if env:
        return env
    here = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
    root = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(here, "..", "..", ".."))
    d = os.path.join(root, "sim", "notes")
    if os.path.exists(os.path.join(root, ".git")) and os.path.isdir(d):
        return os.path.join(d, "relay-log.md")
    return None


def read_relay():
    """What the relay log says, headings and field lines only; entry text is never read
    into the result. Returns a dict with ok, why, entries (R-n -> list of entries in writer
    form), outcomes, legacy (headings that begin '## R-' and are not in writer form) and
    newest. The read is under a shared flock on relay-log's own lock file, with a timeout:
    a writer holds it exclusively while it numbers and appends."""
    out = {"ok": False, "why": "", "entries": {}, "outcomes": [], "legacy": 0, "newest": None}
    path = relay_path()
    if not path:
        out["why"] = "no relay log path (set RELAY_LOG)"
        return out
    if not os.path.isfile(path):
        out["why"] = f"no relay log at {path}"
        return out
    lock = None
    if os.path.exists(path + ".lock"):
        try:
            lock = open(path + ".lock", "r")
        except OSError:
            lock = None
    try:
        if lock is not None:
            deadline = time.monotonic() + RELAY_LOCK_TIMEOUT
            while True:
                try:
                    fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_SH | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
                    break
                except BlockingIOError:
                    if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
                        out["why"] = f"relay lock {path}.lock held for more than {RELAY_LOCK_TIMEOUT:.0f}s"
                        return out
                    time.sleep(0.05)
        try:
            with open(path, "rb") as f:
                text = f.read().decode("utf-8", errors="replace")
        except OSError as err:
            out["why"] = f"relay log unreadable: {err.strerror}"
            return out
    finally:
        if lock is not None:
            lock.close()
    lines = text.split("\n")
    for i, line in enumerate(lines):
        m = RELAY_HEAD.match(line)
        if m:
            ws = []
            fm = WS_FIELD.match(lines[i + 1]) if i + 1 < len(lines) else None
            if fm:
                ws = [w for w in (x.strip() for x in fm.group(1).split(",")) if SLUG.match(w)]
            intake = None
            for nxt in lines[i + 1:i + 4]:
                im = INTAKE_FIELD.match(nxt)
                if im:
                    intake = im.group(1)
                    break
                if nxt.startswith("**Text, verbatim:**"):
                    break
            out["entries"].setdefault(int(m.group(1)), []).append({"n": int(m.group(1)), "stamp": m.group(2), "to": m.group(3).strip(), "ws": ws, "intake": intake})
            if out["newest"] is None or m.group(2) > out["newest"]:
                out["newest"] = m.group(2)
            continue
        m = RELAY_OUTCOME.match(line)
        if m:
            out["outcomes"].append((int(m.group(1)), m.group(2)))
        elif line.startswith("## R-"):
            out["legacy"] += 1
    out["ok"] = True
    return out


def unique_entry(relay, n):
    """The one writer-form entry numbered n, or None when there is none or two."""
    es = relay["entries"].get(n, [])
    return es[0] if len(es) == 1 else None


def relay_events(row, relay, t_now):
    """The observe events the relay log gives one row that the row has not consumed."""
    nums = {}
    for n, es in relay["entries"].items():
        e = unique_entry(relay, n)
        if e and row["slug"] in e["ws"]:
            nums[n] = e
    for link in row["links"]:
        if RELAY_LINK.match(link):
            n = int(link[len("relay:R-"):])
            e = unique_entry(relay, n)
            if e:
                nums[n] = e
    facts = []
    for n, e in sorted(nums.items()):
        facts.append((f"relay:R-{n}@{e['stamp']}", e["stamp"]))
    for n, st in relay["outcomes"]:
        if n in nums:
            facts.append((f"relay:R-{n}/outcome@{st}", st))
    events = []
    for src, st in facts:
        if src in row["consumed"]:
            continue
        events.append({"event": "observe", "ws": row["slug"], "src": src, "moved_at": min(st, t_now), "checked_at": t_now})
    return events


def desk_snapshot():
    """(snapshot, None) when fresh and readable, else (None, why). The same bound as K13."""
    try:
        with open(SNAPSHOT, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            snap = json.load(f)
        read_at = parse_time(snap["read_at"])
        open_ids = snap["open"]
        if not isinstance(open_ids, list):
            raise ValueError("open is not a list")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None, "UNREAD: no snapshot"
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
        return None, "UNREAD: the snapshot cannot be read"
    hours = (parse_time(now()) - read_at).total_seconds() / 3600
    if hours < 0 or hours > THRESHOLD_HOURS["desk snapshot"]:
        return None, f"UNREAD: the snapshot read at {snap['read_at']} is outside {THRESHOLD_HOURS['desk snapshot']}h"
    return snap, None


def card_status(snap, card):
    ids = snap.get("ids")
    if isinstance(ids, dict):
        st = ids.get(card)
        return st if isinstance(st, str) else None
    return "open" if card in snap["open"] else None


def desk_events(row, snap, t_now, gaps):
    events = []
    cards = []
    for link in row["links"]:
        if not ASK.match(link):
            continue
        card = link[4:]
        st = card_status(snap, card)
        cards.append((card, st))
        if st is None:
            gaps.append(f"{row['slug']}: card {card} is not on the Desk (snapshot read {snap['read_at']})")
            continue
        src = f"desk:{card}@{snap['read_at']}"
        if src in row["consumed"]:
            continue
        events.append({"event": "observe", "ws": row["slug"], "link": link,
                       "seen": {"kind": "desk", "state": st, "read_at": snap["read_at"]},
                       "src": src, "checked_at": t_now})
    # LF4: the card is the one source for "blocked on the operator" (K13), so when it closes
    # the block clears. Links only accumulate, and the row does not record which of its cards
    # set the current block, so the clear needs every ask: card on the row in a closing status:
    # an old closed card never clears a block a later, still open card holds (review 5644084635).
    # A card absent from the snapshot keeps the block. Only a run that read something new for
    # the row clears it, and the next action stays director's; the hint says so.
    if (events and row["blocked"] == "operator"
            and all(st is not None and st in CLOSING_STATUSES for _, st in cards)):
        events.append({"event": "set", "ws": row["slug"], "blocked": "", "src": events[0]["src"],
                       "hint": "; ".join(f"card {c} is {st}" for c, st in cards) + "; the next action is director's"})
    elif events and row["blocked"] == "operator" and any(st in CLOSING_STATUSES for _, st in cards):
        # Some linked card closed and another holds the block: say which, so a card stuck in
        # yours, or gone from the Desk, does not keep the block silently (review 5644312313).
        for c, st in cards:
            if st not in CLOSING_STATUSES:
                gaps.append(f"{row['slug']}: operator block held by card {c} ({st or 'not on the Desk'}); "
                            f"if that card no longer holds it, director drops the link: dws link {row['slug']} --remove ask:{c}")
    return events


def cmd_refresh_local(a):
    """The source-only refresh (ledger fill): the relay log and the Desk snapshot, no network.
    Reads happen outside the ledger lock and one lock is held at a time; the events are decided
    under the ledger lock against the row as it is then."""
    rows, _ = fold()
    slugs = a.slugs or [r["slug"] for r in sorted_rows(rows)]
    for slug in slugs:
        need(rows, slug)
    t_now = now()
    relay = read_relay()
    snap, desk_why = desk_snapshot()
    gaps = []
    if not relay["ok"]:
        gaps.append(f"relay source unreadable: {relay['why']}")
    if snap is None:
        gaps.append(f"Desk {desk_why}")
    if relay["ok"] and relay["legacy"]:
        gaps.append(f"{relay['legacy']} relay headings not in writer form were not read")

    def plan(current):
        events = []
        for slug in slugs:
            row = current.get(slug)
            if row is None:
                continue
            if relay["ok"]:
                events.extend(relay_events(row, relay, t_now))
            if snap is not None:
                events.extend(desk_events(row, snap, t_now, gaps))
        return events

    events = write_many("refresh", plan, lambda evs: {"event": "refresh-run", "at": t_now, "rows": len(slugs),
                                                      "links": 0, "warnings": len(gaps), "local": True})
    for e in events:
        if e["event"] == "set":
            print(f"{e['ws']}: operator block cleared ({e['src']}); hint: {e['hint']}")
        elif e.get("moved_at"):
            print(f"{e['ws']}: moved {e['moved_at']} ({e['src']})")
        elif e.get("link"):
            print(f"{e['ws']}: {e['link']} is {e['seen']['state']} on the Desk"
                  + (f"; hint: card {e['link'][4:]} is {e['seen']['state']}, the next action is director's" if e["seen"]["state"] in ("yours", "split") else ""))
    for g in gaps:
        print(f"dws refresh --local: {g}", file=sys.stderr)


def cmd_unlinked(a):
    """What the fill could not tie to a row, listed and never guessed. Writes nothing."""
    rows, _ = fold()
    relay = read_relay()
    snap, desk_why = desk_snapshot()
    linked_n = {int(l[len("relay:R-"):]) for r in rows.values() for l in r["links"] if RELAY_LINK.match(l)}
    names = {r["slug"] for r in rows.values()}
    entries = [e for n in sorted(relay["entries"]) for e in relay["entries"][n]]
    if a.since:
        entries = [e for e in entries if e["stamp"][:10] >= a.since]
    unlinked_entries = [e for e in entries if not e["ws"] and e["n"] not in linked_n]
    unknown = sorted({(w, e["n"]) for e in entries for w in e["ws"] if w not in names})
    not_writer = sorted((r["slug"], l) for r in rows.values() for l in r["links"]
                        if RELAY_LINK.match(l) and unique_entry(relay, int(l[len("relay:R-"):])) is None)
    no_link = sorted(r["slug"] for r in rows.values() if not r["links"])
    op_nocard = sorted(r["slug"] for r in rows.values() if operator_blocked(r["blocked"]) and not any(ASK.match(l) for l in r["links"]))
    cards_linked = {l[4:] for r in rows.values() for l in r["links"] if ASK.match(l)}
    open_cards = sorted(c for c in (snap["open"] if snap else []) if c not in cards_linked)
    sources = {
        "relay": ({"newest_entry": relay["newest"], "legacy_headings": relay["legacy"]} if relay["ok"] else {"UNREAD": relay["why"]}),
        "desk": ({"read_at": snap["read_at"]} if snap else {"UNREAD": desk_why}),
        "ask_ledger": {"not_read": "W5 is not built"},
    }
    if a.json:
        json.dump({"relay_entries_without_workstream": [{"n": e["n"], "stamp": e["stamp"], "to": e["to"]} for e in unlinked_entries],
                   "unknown_workstream_names": [{"ws": w, "entry": n} for w, n in unknown],
                   "relay_links_not_in_writer_form": [{"ws": w, "link": l} for w, l in not_writer],
                   "rows_with_no_link": no_link, "rows_blocked_on_operator_with_no_card": op_nocard,
                   "open_desk_cards_no_row_links": open_cards, "sources": sources}, sys.stdout, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)
        print()
        return
    print("relay entries in writer form with no workstream:")
    for e in unlinked_entries:
        print(f"  R-{e['n']} {e['stamp']} -> {e['to']}")
    print("workstream names that match no row:")
    for w, n in unknown:
        print(f"  {w} (R-{n})")
    print("relay links not in writer form:")
    for w, l in not_writer:
        print(f"  {w} {l} (no writer-form entry has this number)")
    print(f"rows with no link: {len(no_link)}")
    for w in no_link:
        print(f"  {w}")
    print("rows blocked on the operator with no card link:")
    for w in op_nocard:
        print(f"  {w}")
    print("open Desk cards that no row links:")
    for c in open_cards:
        print(f"  {c}")
    print("sources:")
    print("  relay: " + (f"newest entry stamped {relay['newest'] or 'none'} (the log's own time, not when it was read); {relay['legacy']} headings not in writer form" if relay["ok"] else f"UNREAD ({relay['why']})"))
    print("  Desk: " + (f"snapshot read {snap['read_at']}" if snap else desk_why))
    print("  ask ledger: not read (W5 is not built)")


def last_refresh(path=LEDGER):
    """The newest refresh-run event (the run record refresh appends last, local or not), or None.
    The fold ignores these events for every row; only this read and `show --json` use them."""
    best = None
    try:
        f = open(path, "rb")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None
    with f:
        for line in f:
            if b"refresh-run" not in line:
                continue
            try:
                e = json.loads(line.decode("utf-8"))
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("event") == "refresh-run" and isinstance(e.get("at"), str):
                if best is None or e["at"] >= best["at"]:
                    best = {k: e[k] for k in ("at", "rows", "links", "warnings", "local") if k in e}
    return best


def waits_state(state):
    """D2: a decision edge as the reader sees it. A confirm meets it; a withdrawn record ends it."""
    return {"confirmed": "met", "withdrawn": "ended", None: "unknown"}.get(state, "waiting" if state in DECISION_OPEN else state)


# ---- intake: one ask id from the moment an operator ask arrives -------------------------------
# `intake` mints the id and records the ask; relay-log --ask, card-ingest --intake and a row's
# intake:I-<n> link carry it onward, and `asks` joins them. The record is
# $DIRECTOR_STATE/asks.jsonl, one line {ask_id, received_at, text, source}, appended under one
# flock like relay-log's. The time is the clock's; there is no argument to set it.
ASKS = os.path.join(STATE, "asks.jsonl")
ASKS_LOCK = os.path.join(STATE, "asks.lock")
NONE = "none"


def read_asks(path=None):
    """The ask records in file order, torn or malformed lines skipped."""
    out = []
    try:
        f = open(path or ASKS, "rb")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return out
    with f:
        for line in f:
            try:
                e = json.loads(line.decode("utf-8"))
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if isinstance(e, dict) and isinstance(e.get("ask_id"), str) and INTAKE_ID.match(e["ask_id"]):
                out.append(e)
    return out


def cmd_intake(a):
    if a.text_file == "-":
        text = sys.stdin.read()
    else:
        try:
            with open(a.text_file, encoding="utf-8") as f:
                text = f.read()
        except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError) as err:
            raise Refused(f"cannot read {a.text_file}: {getattr(err, 'strerror', None) or err}")
    if not text.strip():
        raise Refused("the ask text is empty; nothing written")
    if not SLUG.match(a.source):
        raise Refused(f"--source {a.source!r} must be lower case letters, digits, '.', '_' or '-'")
    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    fd = os.open(ASKS_LOCK, os.O_CREAT | os.O_RDWR, 0o600)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        nums = [int(e["ask_id"][2:]) for e in read_asks()]
        ask_id = f"I-{(max(nums) if nums else 0) + 1}"
        append({"ask_id": ask_id, "received_at": now(), "text": text.rstrip("\n"), "source": a.source}, ASKS)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    print(ask_id)


def cmd_asks(a):
    """One row per ask: id, received_at, card, answer time, relay, row. A blank is 'none'; several
    values join with a comma in sorted order, so the same inputs give the same bytes."""
    try:
        with open(SNAPSHOT, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            snap = json.load(f)
        if not isinstance(snap, dict):
            snap = {}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        snap = {}
    cards_of, answered_at = {}, snap.get("answered_at") if isinstance(snap.get("answered_at"), dict) else {}
    intake_map = snap.get("intake") if isinstance(snap.get("intake"), dict) else {}
    for card, ask in intake_map.items():
        cards_of.setdefault(ask, []).append(card)
    relay = read_relay()
    relays_of = {}
    for n, es in relay["entries"].items():
        for e in es:
            if e.get("intake"):
                relays_of.setdefault(e["intake"], []).append(n)
    rows, _ = fold()
    rows_of = {}
    for r in rows.values():
        for link in r["links"]:
            if INTAKE_LINK.match(link):
                rows_of.setdefault(link[len("intake:"):], []).append(r["slug"])

    def join(values):
        return ",".join(values) if values else NONE
    out = []
    for e in sorted(read_asks(), key=lambda e: int(e["ask_id"][2:])):
        i = e["ask_id"]
        cards = sorted(cards_of.get(i, []))
        times = sorted(answered_at[c] for c in cards if isinstance(answered_at.get(c), str))
        out.append({"ask_id": i, "received_at": e.get("received_at") or NONE, "card": join(cards),
                    "answered_at": ",".join(times) if times else NONE,
                    "relay": join([f"R-{n}" for n in sorted(set(relays_of.get(i, [])))]),
                    "row": join(sorted(rows_of.get(i, [])))})
    if a.json:
        json.dump(out, sys.stdout, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True)
        print()
        return
    cols = ("ask", "received_at", "card", "answered_at", "relay", "row")
    keys = ("ask_id", "received_at", "card", "answered_at", "relay", "row")
    table = [cols] + [tuple(r[k] for k in keys) for r in out]
    widths = [max(len(c[i]) for c in table) for i in range(len(cols))]
    for row in table:
        print("  ".join(c.ljust(w) for c, w in zip(row, widths)).rstrip())


# ---- waiting: the PR half of the standing hook's "waiting:" line --------------------------------
# `waiting write` is the one step that may call gh. It reads the ledger's pr: links, asks gh which of
# those PRs are open and approved, and writes $DIRECTOR_STATE/waiting-prs.json for standing-hook to
# read (the hook reads files only). If any PR cannot be read it writes nothing and says which, so a
# cache is never a silent partial: the old file just ages until the hook reads it as UNKNOWN.
WAITING = os.path.join(STATE, "waiting-prs.json")


def approved_at(d):
    """The time a PR open and approved was approved, else None. Reads reviewDecision and the reviews."""
    if (d.get("state") or "").upper() != "OPEN" or d.get("isDraft"):
        return None
    reviews = [r for r in d.get("reviews") or [] if isinstance(r, dict)]
    times = sorted(r["submittedAt"] for r in reviews if r.get("state") == "APPROVED" and isinstance(r.get("submittedAt"), str))
    decision = d.get("reviewDecision")
    if decision == "APPROVED" or (not decision and times):
        return times[-1] if times else NONE
    return None


def cmd_waiting_write(a):
    rows, _ = fold()
    prs = sorted({(m.group(2), m.group(3)) for r in rows.values() if r["stage"] != "parked"
                  for m in (LINK.match(l) for l in r["links"]) if m and m.group(1) == "pr"})
    waiting, errors = [], []
    for repo, num in prs:
        try:
            d = json.loads(run_json(["gh", "pr", "view", num, "-R", repo, "--json", "state,isDraft,reviewDecision,reviews"]))
        except (RuntimeError, ValueError, OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as err:
            errors.append(f"{repo}#{num}: {str(err).splitlines()[0][:120] if str(err) else type(err).__name__}")
            continue
        at = approved_at(d)
        if at:
            waiting.append({"pr": f"{repo}#{num}", "approved_at": at if at != NONE else None})
    if errors:
        for e in errors:
            print(f"dws: waiting: could not read {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        raise Refused(f"{len(errors)} of {len(prs)} PRs unreadable; {WAITING} not written")
    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=STATE, prefix=".waiting-prs.")
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
            json.dump({"written_at": now(), "checked": len(prs), "approved_not_merged": waiting}, f, indent=1)
            f.write("\n")
            f.flush()
            os.fsync(f.fileno())
        os.replace(tmp, WAITING)
    except BaseException:
        if os.path.exists(tmp):
            os.unlink(tmp)
        raise
    print(f"dws: waiting: {len(waiting)} approved PRs not merged of {len(prs)} checked -> {WAITING}")


def cmd_show(a):
    total = {}
    decisions = {}
    rows, torn = fold(tally=total, decisions=decisions)
    for r in rows.values():
        r["waits_state"] = {did: waits_state(decisions.get(did, {}).get("state")) for did in r["waits"]}
    ordered = sorted_rows(rows)
    if a.json:
        json.dump({"ledger": LEDGER, "torn": torn, "tags": total, "last_refresh": last_refresh(), "rows": ordered}, sys.stdout, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)
        print()
    else:
        cols = ("stage", "workstream", "owner", "last moved", "blocked on", "next action", "links")
        table = [cols] + [(r["stage"], r["slug"], r["owner"], r["last_moved"], r["blocked"], r["next"], " ".join(r["links"])) for r in ordered]
        widths = [max(len(str(row[i])) for row in table) for i in range(len(cols))]
        for row in table:
            print("  ".join(str(c).ljust(w) for c, w in zip(row, widths)).rstrip())
    if torn:
        print(f"dws: {torn} unreadable line(s) in {LEDGER} skipped, not repaired", file=sys.stderr)

# K19: the board's generated state section (sim/design/director-functions-redesign.md,
# section 4, "Board"). `board-state` rewrites only the text between the two markers
# in $DIRECTOR_STATE/board.md, from the ledger and the Desk snapshot; the authored
# narrative around it is never touched. With no markers the block is put at the top.
# A malformed pair is refused and nothing is written. `board-check` lists the ask: and
# ws: ids in the prose that resolve to no record; it exits 0 (a diagnostic, SOUL
# section 8), and an id whose store is UNREAD is "not checked", never "unresolved".
BOARD_BEGIN = "<!-- state:begin -->"
BOARD_END = "<!-- state:end -->"
BOARD_TOKEN = re.compile(r"\b(ask|ws):([A-Za-z0-9](?:[A-Za-z0-9._-]*[A-Za-z0-9])?)")


def board_path():
    return os.path.join(STATE, "board.md")


def board_markers(lines):
    """(begin, end) line indexes of the one generated block, (None, None) when there is none.
    Anything else (a lone marker, two blocks, the end first) is refused: dws never guesses
    which text is generated."""
    begins = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.rstrip("\r\n") == BOARD_BEGIN]
    ends = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.rstrip("\r\n") == BOARD_END]
    if not begins and not ends:
        return None, None
    if len(begins) != 1 or len(ends) != 1 or ends[0] < begins[0]:
        raise Refused(f"{board_path()} has {len(begins)} begin and {len(ends)} end marker(s); it needs "
                      f"none, or exactly one {BOARD_BEGIN} followed by one {BOARD_END}. Nothing was written")
    return begins[0], ends[0]


def board_sources():
    """The two stores the board reads: (rows or None, ledger source, snapshot or None, desk source)."""
    rows, lsrc = None, {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"no ledger at {LEDGER}"}
    if os.path.isfile(LEDGER):
        rows, torn = fold()
        if not rows and (torn or ledger_has_lines()):
            rows, lsrc = None, {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"{LEDGER} has no readable row (torn {torn})"}
        else:
            lsrc = {"state": "read", "torn": torn}
    snap, why = desk_snapshot()
    dsrc = {"state": "read", "read_at": snap["read_at"]} if snap else {"state": "UNREAD", "why": why}
    return rows, lsrc, snap, dsrc


def board_block(t_now):
    rows, lsrc, snap, dsrc = board_sources()
    out = [BOARD_BEGIN,
           f"## State (generated {t_now} by dws board-state; it is rewritten, so edit the text outside these markers)"]
    ltxt = f"read {t_now}" + (f" (torn {lsrc['torn']})" if lsrc.get("torn") else "") if lsrc["state"] == "read" else f"UNREAD ({lsrc['why']})"
    dtxt = f"read {dsrc['read_at']}" if dsrc["state"] == "read" else f"UNREAD ({dsrc['why']})"
    out.append(f"sources: ledger {ltxt}; desk {dtxt}")
    out.append(f"open Desk cards: {len(snap['open']) if snap else 'UNREAD'}")
    if rows is None:
        out.append("rows: UNREAD")
    else:
        by = {}
        for r in rows.values():
            by[r["stage"]] = by.get(r["stage"], 0) + 1
        order = [st for st in STAGES if st in by] + sorted(st for st in by if st not in STAGES)
        out.append(f"rows: {len(rows)}" + (" (" + ", ".join(f"{st} {by[st]}" for st in order) + ")" if by else ""))
        for r in sorted_rows(rows):
            asks = " ".join(l for l in r["links"] if ASK.match(l))
            blocked = f"  blocked on {stored_form(r['blocked'])}" if r["blocked"] else ""
            out.append(f"- {r['slug']}  {r['stage']}  {r['owner'] or 'no owner'}  moved {r['last_moved']}{blocked}" + (f"  {asks}" if asks else ""))
    out.append(BOARD_END)
    return out


def cmd_board_state(a):
    path = board_path()
    if not os.path.isfile(path):
        raise Refused(f"no board at {path}; the board is authored and dws never creates it")
    with Locked(path + ".lock"):
        with open(path, "rb") as f:
            raw = f.read()
        lines = raw.decode("utf-8", errors="surrogateescape").splitlines(keepends=True)
        begin, end = board_markers(lines)
        # the board's own line ending: CRLF when its first line ends in one, so a board
        # kept with CRLF is not left half converted
        eol = "\r\n" if lines and lines[0].endswith("\r\n") else "\n"
        block = [l + eol for l in board_block(now())]
        if begin is None:
            new = block + [eol] + lines
        else:
            new = lines[:begin] + block + lines[end + 1:]
        data = "".join(new).encode("utf-8", errors="surrogateescape")
        if data != raw:
            fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=os.path.dirname(path), prefix=".board.md.tmp")
            try:
                os.fchmod(fd, os.stat(path).st_mode & 0o7777)
                with os.fdopen(fd, "wb") as f:
                    f.write(data)
                    f.flush()
                    os.fsync(f.fileno())
                os.replace(tmp, path)
            except BaseException:
                try:
                    os.unlink(tmp)
                except OSError:
                    pass
                raise
    print(f"dws: wrote the state block in {path}")


def cmd_board_check(a):
    path = board_path()
    if not os.path.isfile(path):
        raise Refused(f"no board at {path}")
    with open(path, "rb") as f:
        lines = f.read().decode("utf-8", errors="replace").splitlines()
    try:
        begin, end = board_markers(lines)
        note = None
    except Refused as err:
        begin, end, note = None, None, str(err)
    rows, lsrc, snap, dsrc = board_sources()
    ids = snap.get("ids") if snap and isinstance(snap.get("ids"), dict) else None
    unresolved, not_checked, checked = [], [], 0
    for n, line in enumerate(lines, 1):
        if begin is not None and begin <= n - 1 <= end:
            continue
        for m in BOARD_TOKEN.finditer(line):
            kind, ident = m.group(1), m.group(2)
            token = f"{kind}:{ident}"
            item = {"token": token, "line": n}
            if kind == "ask":
                if snap is None or ids is None:
                    not_checked.append({**item, "why": "the Desk snapshot is UNREAD"})
                    continue
                resolved = ident in ids
            else:
                if rows is None:
                    not_checked.append({**item, "why": "the ledger is UNREAD"})
                    continue
                resolved = ident in rows
            checked += 1
            if not resolved:
                unresolved.append(item)
    report = {"board": path, "sources": {"ledger": lsrc, "desk": dsrc}, "checked": checked,
              "unresolved": unresolved, "not_checked": not_checked}
    if note:
        report["marker_problem"] = note
    if a.json:
        json.dump(report, sys.stdout, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)
        print()
        return
    if note:
        print(f"note: {note}; the whole board was read as prose")
    print(f"board-check: {checked} id(s) checked, {len(unresolved)} unresolved, {len(not_checked)} not checked")
    for u in unresolved:
        print(f"unresolved   board.md:{u['line']}  {u['token']}")
    for u in not_checked:
        print(f"not checked  board.md:{u['line']}  {u['token']} ({u['why']})")


# K12: `queue`, the operator's queue with the presentation check applied (design
# section 4, Q2 and Q5 as ruled). It reads the Desk snapshot and joins each open card
# to the ledger rows that link it (ask:<id>). A card is hidden only when it links at
# least one PR and every linked PR is observed draft, merged or closed (R-171, R-198;
# Q5 c: the ask stays open until director closes it, and the queue hides it till then).
# Every other open card is shown, and a card no row links is "unclassified, shown"
# (Q2: no cap). The snapshot holds no card kind, text or source, so the clerical-relay
# check (R-203), the no-source check and the grouping into merges, rulings and console
# steps are listed as "check not run", never guessed. Read only.
QUEUE_HIDDEN_PR = ("draft", "merged", "closed")
QUEUE_NOT_RUN = [
    {"check": "grouping by kind", "why": "the Desk snapshot holds no card kind"},
    {"check": "clerical relay", "why": "the Desk snapshot holds no card text (R-203)"},
    {"check": "claims with no source", "why": "the Desk snapshot holds no card source"},
]


def queue_report():
    """The queue as data: (report, snapshot). cmd_queue prints it; the digest reads it."""
    rows, lsrc, snap, dsrc = board_sources()
    torn = lsrc.get("torn", 0) if lsrc["state"] == "read" else 0
    report = {"sources": {"ledger": lsrc, "desk": dsrc}, "shown": None, "hidden": None, "counts": None,
              "not_run": QUEUE_NOT_RUN}
    if snap is not None:
        shown, hidden = [], []
        for card in sorted(snap["open"]):
            linked = [] if rows is None else [r for r in sorted(rows.values(), key=lambda r: r["slug"])
                                              if f"ask:{card}" in r["links"]]
            if not linked:
                shown.append({"card": card, "kind": "unclassified",
                              "note": "no ledger row links it" if rows is not None else "the ledger is UNREAD"})
                continue
            prs, unread = [], []
            for r in linked:
                for l in r["links"]:
                    if l.startswith("pr:"):
                        o = r["observed"].get(l)
                        st = (o.get("seen") or {}).get("state") if isinstance(o, dict) else None
                        (prs if st else unread).append({"ws": r["slug"], "link": l, "state": st,
                                                       "checked_at": o.get("checked_at") if isinstance(o, dict) else None})
            first = linked[0]
            if prs and not unread and all(p["state"] in QUEUE_HIDDEN_PR for p in prs):
                p = prs[0]
                if torn:
                    # a torn ledger line may hold a PR state (a ready observation that would
                    # have kept this card), so nothing is hidden on a ledger that is not whole
                    shown.append({"card": card, "kind": "row", "ws": first["slug"], "stage": first["stage"],
                                  "note": f"would be hidden ({p['state']}); shown because a torn ledger line may hold a PR state (hiding stays off until that line of workstreams.jsonl is fixed or removed)"})
                    continue
                hidden.append({"card": card, "ws": p["ws"], "why": {"link": p["link"], "state": p["state"], "checked_at": p["checked_at"]}})
                continue
            item = {"card": card, "kind": "row", "ws": first["slug"], "stage": first["stage"]}
            if unread:
                item["note"] = "PR state unread"
            shown.append(item)
        report.update({"shown": shown, "hidden": hidden,
                       "counts": {"open": len(snap["open"]), "shown": len(shown), "hidden": len(hidden)}})
    return report, snap


def cmd_queue(a):
    report, snap = queue_report()
    lsrc, dsrc = report["sources"]["ledger"], report["sources"]["desk"]
    if a.json:
        json.dump(report, sys.stdout, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)
        print()
        return
    ltxt = ("read" + (f" (torn {lsrc['torn']})" if lsrc.get("torn") else "")) if lsrc["state"] == "read" else f"UNREAD ({lsrc['why']})"
    if snap is None:
        print(f"queue    UNREAD ({dsrc['why']}); ledger {ltxt}")
    else:
        print(f"queue    desk read {dsrc['read_at']}; ledger {ltxt}")
        c = report["counts"]
        print(f"shown {c['shown']} of {c['open']} open card(s)")
        for x in report["shown"]:
            where = f"unclassified ({x['note']})" if x["kind"] == "unclassified" else f"on {x['ws']} ({x['stage']})" + (f"; {x['note']}" if x.get("note") else "")
            print(f"  {x['card']}  {where}")
        print(f"hidden {c['hidden']} (shown again only if a linked PR is observed ready; gone once director closes the card)")
        for x in report["hidden"]:
            w = x["why"]
            print(f"  {x['card']}  on {x['ws']}: {w['link']} is {w['state']} (checked {w['checked_at']})")
    for n in QUEUE_NOT_RUN:
        print(f"not run  {n['check']}: {n['why']}")


# K18: `digest`, the operator digest and the close-or-kill list, rendered on demand from the
# reconciler and the queue (design rows 8 and 9; Q1 and Q7 as ruled). Nothing runs it on a
# clock: a session runs it. It prints to stdout and writes the same text to
# $DIRECTOR_STATE/digest.md and nothing else: it builds the reconciler's report in memory
# (reconcile_report) and does not write reconcile-proposals.json. The interrupt list below is the Q1 default list
# (b), a default for the operator to edit here: an outage; a console step or a
# recommendation expiring before the next digest; a seat blocked on your ask. An item whose
# source a script cannot read is "check not run", and one whose store is UNREAD says UNREAD;
# neither is ever read as "none".
DIGEST_INTERRUPTS = (
    ("an outage", "no outage source a script can read"),
    ("a console step or a recommendation expiring before the next digest",
     "the Desk snapshot holds no card expiry and recommendations have no store"),
    ("a seat blocked on your ask", None),
)


def cmd_digest(a):
    t_now = now()
    rec, _ = reconcile_report()
    queue, snap = queue_report()
    rows, lsrc, _, _ = board_sources()
    src = rec["sources"]

    def stext(v):
        return f"read {v['read_at']}" if v["state"] == "read" else f"UNREAD ({v['why']})"

    out = [f"# Digest, generated {t_now} by dws digest (on demand)", "",
           "sources: " + "; ".join(f"{k} {stext(v)}" for k, v in sorted(src.items())), "",
           "## Interrupts",
           "The default list (Q1 b); the operator edits DIGEST_INTERRUPTS in dws."]
    for item, why in DIGEST_INTERRUPTS:
        if why is not None:
            out.append(f"- {item}: check not run ({why})")
        elif snap is None or rows is None:
            out.append(f"- {item}: UNREAD ({'the Desk snapshot' if snap is None else 'the ledger'} is UNREAD)")
        else:
            blocked = [f"{r['slug']} (card {l[4:]})" for r in sorted_rows(rows) if operator_blocked(r["blocked"])
                       for l in r["links"] if ASK.match(l) and l[4:] in snap["open"]]
            out.append(f"- {item}: " + (", ".join(blocked) if blocked else "none"))
    out += ["", "## Queue"]
    if queue["counts"] is None:
        out.append(f"UNREAD ({queue['sources']['desk']['why']})")
    else:
        c = queue["counts"]
        out.append(f"{c['open']} open, {c['shown']} shown, {c['hidden']} hidden by the presentation check (dws queue lists them)")
    out += ["", "## Close-or-kill"]
    unmoved = [p for p in rec["proposals"] if p["kind"] == "unmoved"]
    if any(n["check"] == "unmoved" for n in rec["not_run"]):
        out.append("UNREAD (the ledger is UNREAD)")
    elif not unmoved:
        out.append("none")
    for p in unmoved:
        ev = p.get("evidence", {})
        out.append(f"- {p['subject']}  {ev.get('stage', '')}  {p['why']}")
    out += ["", "## Other proposals"]
    others = [p for p in rec["proposals"] if p["kind"] != "unmoved"]
    if not others:
        out.append("none")
    for p in others:
        out.append(f"- {p['kind']}: {p['subject']}  {p['why']}")
    out += ["", "## Not run"]
    for n in rec["not_run"] + queue["not_run"]:
        out.append(f"- {n['check']}: {n['why']}")
    text = "\n".join(out) + "\n"
    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    path = os.path.join(STATE, "digest.md")
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=STATE, prefix=".digest.md.tmp")
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            f.write(text)
            f.flush()
            os.fsync(f.fileno())
        os.replace(tmp, path)
    except BaseException:
        try:
            os.unlink(tmp)
        except OSError:
            pass
        raise
    sys.stdout.write(text)


# K9: rulings.jsonl, the store of rulings, grants and terms (R-201, R-204, R-184).
# The file is the one merge-guard reads for exclusions (R-153); exclusions stay
# the operator's and dws never writes one. The operator creates the file, so dws
# refuses when it is missing and never creates it. Its lock is its own file beside it.
RECORD_KINDS = ("ruling", "grant", "exclusion", "term")
RECORD_ID = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]*")
RECORD_DATE = re.compile(r"\d{4}-\d\d-\d\d(T\d\d:\d\d:\d\dZ)?")


def rulings_path():
    return os.environ.get("MERGE_GUARD_RULINGS") or os.path.join(STATE, "rulings.jsonl")


def need_file(path):
    if not os.path.exists(path):
        raise Refused(f"no rulings file at {path}; the guard cannot tell no exclusions declared from a record that "
                      "is gone (R-153). The operator creates the file and enters their exclusions (an empty file "
                      "means none declared); a seat reports this and does not create the file")
    if not os.path.isfile(path):
        raise Refused(f"the rulings path {path} exists and is not a file")


def ledger_has_lines():
    """True when the ledger holds any non-blank line: lines that all parse but fold to no row
    are not an empty ledger."""
    with open(LEDGER, "rb") as f:
        return any(l.strip() for l in f)


def fold_records(path):
    """The records in file order, each with replaced_by (the ids whose replaces
    names it), how many lines could not be read, and the replaces pointers that
    resolve to nothing or to another kind. A pointer is never guessed at."""
    records, torn = [], 0
    try:
        f = open(path, "rb")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return records, 0, []
    with f:
        for line in f:
            if not line.strip():
                continue
            try:
                e = json.loads(line.decode("utf-8"))
            except ValueError:
                torn += 1
                continue
            if not isinstance(e, dict):
                torn += 1
                continue
            records.append({**e, "replaced_by": []})
    by_id = {}
    for r in records:
        if isinstance(r.get("id"), str):
            by_id.setdefault(r["id"], r)
    unresolved = []
    for r in records:
        ptr = r.get("replaces")
        if ptr is None:
            continue
        target = by_id.get(ptr) if isinstance(ptr, str) else None
        if target is None:
            unresolved.append({"id": r.get("id"), "replaces": ptr, "why": "missing"})
        elif target.get("kind") != r.get("kind"):
            unresolved.append({"id": r.get("id"), "replaces": ptr, "why": "other kind"})
        else:
            target["replaced_by"].append(r.get("id"))
    return records, torn, unresolved


def nonblank(field, value):
    if value is None or not value.strip():
        raise Refused(f"--{field.replace('_', '-')} is required and may not be blank")
    return value


def record_date(field, value):
    m = RECORD_DATE.fullmatch(value)
    try:
        if not m:
            raise ValueError
        datetime.datetime.strptime(value, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ" if m.group(1) else "%Y-%m-%d")
    except ValueError:
        raise Refused(f"{field} {value!r} is not a date (YYYY-MM-DD or YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ)")
    return value


def record_id(field, value):
    if not RECORD_ID.fullmatch(value):
        raise Refused(f"{field} {value!r} is not an id")
    return value


def cmd_record(a):
    if a.kind == "exclusion":
        raise Refused("exclusions stay the operator's (R-153): the operator enters them in the rulings file; "
                      "dws writes ruling, grant and term only")
    if a.actor != "director":
        raise Refused(f"actor {a.actor!r} may not write a record; only director does")
    # The text is the operator's words and is stored as given, never normalized (R-186).
    fields = {"source": stored_form(nonblank("source", a.source))}
    if a.kind == "ruling":
        fields.update(subject=stored_form(nonblank("subject", a.subject)), text=nonblank("text", a.text),
                      by=checked("by", nonblank("by", a.by)), ruled_at=record_date("ruled_at", nonblank("ruled_at", a.ruled_at)))
    elif a.kind == "grant":
        if a.state not in ("draft", "confirmed"):
            raise Refused(f"--state {a.state!r} must be draft or confirmed")
        fields.update(subject=stored_form(nonblank("subject", a.subject)), scope=stored_form(nonblank("scope", a.scope)),
                      to=checked("to", nonblank("to", a.to)), state=a.state, text=nonblank("text", a.text))
        if a.expires is not None:
            fields["expires"] = record_date("expires", a.expires)
    else:
        fields.update(role=checked("role", nonblank("role", a.role)), subject=stored_form(nonblank("subject", a.subject)),
                      text=nonblank("text", a.text), set_by=checked("set_by", nonblank("set_by", a.set_by)))
    if getattr(a, "card", None) is not None:
        fields["card"] = record_id("card", a.card)
    if getattr(a, "link", None):
        fields["links"] = [stored_form(x) for x in a.link]
    if a.replaces is not None:
        fields["replaces"] = record_id("replaces", a.replaces)
    tag = "proposal" if a.kind == "grant" and a.state == "draft" else "mirror"
    path = rulings_path()
    need_file(path)
    with Locked(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(path) or ".", "rulings.lock")):
        records, _, _ = fold_records(path)
        ts = now()
        taken = {r.get("id") for r in records}
        if a.id is not None:
            rid = record_id("id", a.id)
        else:
            # The default is <kind>-<UTC ts>; a second record of the same kind in the
            # same second takes -2, -3 and so on, so the id stays unique.
            rid, n = f"{a.kind}-{ts}", 1
            while rid in taken:
                n += 1
                rid = f"{a.kind}-{ts}-{n}"
        if a.replaces is not None and a.replaces == rid:
            raise Refused(f"id {rid!r} replaces itself; nothing written")
        if rid in taken:
            raise Refused(f"id {rid!r} is already in {path}; nothing written")
        append({"kind": a.kind, "id": rid, "ts": ts, "actor": a.actor, "tag": tag, **fields}, path)
    print(f"dws: wrote {a.kind} {rid}")


def cmd_records(a):
    path = rulings_path()
    need_file(path)
    records, torn, unresolved = fold_records(path)
    counts = {}
    for r in records:
        k = r.get("kind") if r.get("kind") in RECORD_KINDS else "unknown"
        counts[k] = counts.get(k, 0) + 1
    if a.kind:
        records = [r for r in records if r.get("kind") == a.kind]
    if a.json:
        json.dump({"file": path, "torn": torn, "counts": counts, "records": records,
                   "unresolved_replaces": unresolved}, sys.stdout, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)
        print()
    else:
        for r in records:
            mark = f"  replaced by {', '.join(map(str, r['replaced_by']))}" if r["replaced_by"] else ""
            print(f"{r.get('kind', '?')}  {r.get('id', '-')}  {r.get('subject', r.get('repo', ''))}{mark}")
        for u in unresolved:
            print(f"unresolved replaces: {u['id']} -> {u['replaces']} ({u['why']})")
    if torn:
        print(f"dws: {torn} unreadable line(s) in {path} skipped, not repaired", file=sys.stderr)


# K15: `inherit <role>`, the by-role read a successor makes (R-204). Read only.
# Standing terms and the grants made to the role come from rulings.jsonl, the
# open asks from the ledger rows the role owns that link a card open on the Desk.
# A source that cannot be read is UNREAD and its section is None, never empty.
# The role is matched as stored: the same string the term, grant or row carries.
def grant_end(g):
    exp = g.get("expires")
    if not isinstance(exp, str):
        return None
    try:
        end = datetime.datetime.strptime(exp, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ" if "T" in exp else "%Y-%m-%d").replace(tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    # A date-only expiry holds through the end of that day, as in reconcile.
    return end if "T" in exp else end + datetime.timedelta(days=1)


def cmd_inherit(a):
    role = checked("role", a.role)
    when = parse_time(now())
    sources = {}
    path = rulings_path()
    terms = replaced_terms = grants = pending = expired = unchecked = None
    if os.path.isfile(path):
        records, rtorn, _ = fold_records(path)
        if rtorn and not records:
            sources["rulings"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"{path} has no readable record (torn {rtorn})"}
        else:
            sources["rulings"] = {"state": "read", "read_at": now(), "torn": rtorn}
    else:
        records = []
        sources["rulings"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"no rulings file at {path}"}
    if sources["rulings"]["state"] == "read":
        terms, replaced_terms, grants, pending, expired, unchecked = [], [], [], [], [], []
        for r in records:
            if r.get("kind") == "term" and r.get("role") == role:
                if r["replaced_by"]:
                    replaced_terms.append({"id": r.get("id"), "text": r.get("text"), "replaced_by": r["replaced_by"]})
                else:
                    terms.append({"id": r.get("id"), "subject": r.get("subject"), "text": r.get("text"), "set_by": r.get("set_by")})
            elif r.get("kind") == "grant" and r.get("to") == role and not r["replaced_by"]:
                item = {"id": r.get("id"), "subject": r.get("subject"), "scope": r.get("scope"),
                        "expires": r.get("expires"), "text": r.get("text")}
                end = grant_end(r)
                if r.get("state") == "draft":
                    pending.append(item)
                elif r.get("state") == "confirmed":
                    if end is None and isinstance(r.get("expires"), str):
                        # reconcile lists this grant as not run; it is not claimed to be in force
                        item["why"] = f"the expiry {r['expires']!r} does not parse"
                        unchecked.append(item)
                    else:
                        (expired if end is not None and end < when else grants).append(item)

    open_asks = None
    snap, why = desk_snapshot()
    sources["desk"] = ({"state": "read", "read_at": snap["read_at"]} if snap else {"state": "UNREAD", "why": why})
    if os.path.isfile(LEDGER):
        rows, ltorn = fold()
        if not rows and (ltorn or ledger_has_lines()):
            sources["ledger"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"{LEDGER} has no readable row (torn {ltorn})"}
        else:
            sources["ledger"] = {"state": "read", "read_at": now(), "torn": ltorn}
        if snap is not None and sources["ledger"]["state"] == "read":
            open_asks = [{"ws": row["slug"], "card": l[4:]} for row in sorted(rows.values(), key=lambda r: r["slug"])
                         if row.get("owner") == role for l in row["links"]
                         if ASK.match(l) and card_status(snap, l[4:]) == "open"]
    else:
        sources["ledger"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"no ledger at {LEDGER}"}

    out = {"role": role, "sources": sources, "terms": terms, "replaced_terms": replaced_terms, "grants": grants,
           "pending_grants": pending, "expired_grants": expired, "unchecked_grants": unchecked,
           "open_asks": open_asks}
    if a.json:
        json.dump(out, sys.stdout, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)
        print()
        return
    for name in ("rulings", "ledger", "desk"):
        v = sources[name]
        print(f"{name:<8} " + (f"read {v['read_at']}" + (f" (torn {v['torn']})" if v.get("torn") else "") if v["state"] == "read" else f"UNREAD  {v['why']}"))

    def section(title, items, fmt):
        if items is None:
            print(f"{title}: UNREAD")
            return
        print(f"{title}: {len(items)}")
        for i in items:
            print("  " + fmt(i))
    section("standing terms", terms, lambda t: f"{t['id']}  {t['text']}")
    section("replaced terms (not standing)", replaced_terms, lambda t: f"{t['id']}  replaced by {', '.join(map(str, t['replaced_by']))}")
    section("grants in force", grants, lambda g: f"{g['id']}  {g['subject']}  scope: {g['scope']}  expires: {g['expires'] or 'no expiry'}")
    section("grants pending confirmation", pending, lambda g: f"{g['id']}  {g['subject']}")
    section("grants with an unparseable expiry (not in force, check not run)", unchecked, lambda g: f"{g['id']}  {g['subject']}  expires: {g['expires']}")
    section("grants expired", expired, lambda g: f"{g['id']}  {g['subject']}  expired {g['expires']}")
    section("open asks", open_asks, lambda x: f"{x['card']}  on {x['ws']}")


# K14: rings.jsonl, keyed by seat (R-200, Q6). A ring, its first turn, its ack and
# its blocker, on the dws store shape: append-only, folded on read, one flock
# (rings.lock) around fold, check and append. Q6's numbers, the operator's: ring
# after 10 minutes idle with mail, at most 3 rings per seat per hour, then report
# the seat as stuck. dws cannot see idleness or mail; the caller states both from
# its own drain, as --actor is a claim. A refused ring writes nothing.
RINGS = os.path.join(STATE, "rings.jsonl")
RING_IDLE_MINUTES = 10
RING_CAP = 3
RING_WINDOW_HOURS = 1
RING_NOTES = ("first-turn", "ack", "blocker")


def rings_lock():
    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    return Locked(os.path.join(STATE, "rings.lock"))


def fold_rings(path=None):
    """Per seat, in file order: every ring time, and the follow-up since the last
    ring (a new ring resets it). Returns (seats, torn)."""
    path = path or RINGS
    seats, torn = {}, 0
    try:
        f = open(path, encoding="utf-8")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return seats, 0
    with f:
        for line in f:
            if not line.strip():
                continue
            try:
                e = json.loads(line)
            except ValueError:
                torn += 1
                continue
            if not isinstance(e, dict) or not isinstance(e.get("seat"), str):
                torn += 1
                continue
            r = seats.setdefault(e["seat"], {"rings": [], "last_ring": None, "first_turn": None,
                                             "ack": None, "blocker": None, "blocker_at": None})
            if e.get("event") == "ring":
                r["rings"].append(e.get("ts", ""))
                r["last_ring"] = e.get("ts", "")
                r["first_turn"] = r["ack"] = r["blocker"] = r["blocker_at"] = None
            elif e.get("event") == "first-turn":
                r["first_turn"] = e.get("ts", "")
            elif e.get("event") == "ack":
                r["ack"] = e.get("ts", "")
            elif e.get("event") == "blocker":
                r["blocker"], r["blocker_at"] = e.get("text", ""), e.get("ts", "")
    return seats, torn


def rings_in_window(r, t_now):
    start = parse_time(t_now) - datetime.timedelta(hours=RING_WINDOW_HOURS)
    return sum(1 for ts in r["rings"] if (parse_ts(ts) or start) > start)


def ring_status(r, t_now):
    if r["ack"]:
        return "acked"
    if rings_in_window(r, t_now) >= RING_CAP:
        return "stuck"
    if r["blocker"]:
        return "blocked"
    if r["first_turn"]:
        return "turned"
    return "rung"


CLAIMS_NOTE = "idle minutes and mail are the caller's claims; dws cannot see either"
_UNSAFE = re.compile("[\x00-\x1f\x7f-\x9f\u061c\u200b-\u200f\u2028-\u202e\u2066-\u2069\ufeff]")


def printable(text):
    """Text from a record, made safe for a terminal: control and bidi runes shown as \\uXXXX."""
    return _UNSAFE.sub(lambda m: "\\u%04x" % ord(m.group()), str(text))


def cmd_ring(a):
    if a.actor != "director":
        raise Refused(f"actor {a.actor!r} may not ring a seat; only director does")
    seat = checked("seat", a.seat)
    if a.idle_minutes < RING_IDLE_MINUTES:
        raise Refused(f"{seat} has been idle {a.idle_minutes} minutes; a ring needs {RING_IDLE_MINUTES} idle (Q6)")
    if a.mail < 1:
        raise Refused(f"{seat} has no mail waiting; a ring needs mail (Q6)")
    t_now = now()
    with rings_lock():
        seats, _ = fold_rings()
        r = seats.get(seat)
        if r and rings_in_window(r, t_now) >= RING_CAP:
            raise Refused(f"{seat} was rung {rings_in_window(r, t_now)} times in the last {RING_WINDOW_HOURS} hour "
                          f"(the cap is {RING_CAP}); report it as stuck, with its blocker if it showed one (Q6)")
        append({"ts": t_now, "actor": a.actor, "event": "ring", "seat": seat,
                "idle_minutes": a.idle_minutes, "mail": a.mail}, RINGS)
    print(f"dws: recorded a ring for {seat} ({CLAIMS_NOTE})")


def cmd_ring_note(a):
    if a.actor != "director":
        raise Refused(f"actor {a.actor!r} may not record a ring follow-up; only director does")
    seat = checked("seat", a.seat)
    text = None
    if a.note == "blocker":
        # The blocker is quoted as the seat showed it (R-200), never normalized.
        text = nonblank("text", a.text)
    elif a.text is not None:
        raise Refused("--text goes with the blocker note only")
    with rings_lock():
        seats, _ = fold_rings()
        if seat not in seats:
            raise Refused(f"no ring recorded for {seat}; there is nothing to follow")
        event = {"ts": now(), "actor": a.actor, "event": a.note, "seat": seat}
        if text is not None:
            event["text"] = text
        append(event, RINGS)
    print(f"dws: recorded {a.note} for {seat}")


def cmd_rings(a):
    seats, torn = fold_rings()
    t_now = now()
    out = {}
    for seat, r in sorted(seats.items()):
        out[seat] = {"status": ring_status(r, t_now), "rings_in_window": rings_in_window(r, t_now),
                     "rings_total": len(r["rings"]), "last_ring": r["last_ring"], "first_turn": r["first_turn"],
                     "ack": r["ack"], "blocker": r["blocker"], "blocker_at": r["blocker_at"]}
    if a.json:
        json.dump({"file": RINGS, "torn": torn, "note": CLAIMS_NOTE, "seats": out}, sys.stdout, indent=2, ensure_ascii=True)
        print()
    else:
        for seat, v in out.items():
            extra = f"  blocker: {printable(v['blocker'])}" if v["blocker"] else ""
            print(f"{printable(seat)}  {v['status']}  rings in the last hour {v['rings_in_window']}  last ring {v['last_ring']}{extra}")
        if out:
            print(f"note: {CLAIMS_NOTE}")
    if torn:
        print(f"dws: {torn} unreadable line(s) in {RINGS} skipped, not repaired", file=sys.stderr)


# K10: the grant confirm card. A draft grant has no effect. grant-card renders a
# Desk card (card-ingest's format) that shows the draft's bounds; the operator
# answers it on the Desk; grant-confirm then records the confirmed grant, and
# only when the fresh Desk snapshot lists that card as answered. dws cannot read
# an answer's content (the snapshot holds only which cards have one), so the
# quote is the session's claim of the operator's words, stored as given, in the
# same way --actor is a claim. The draft line is never edited; the confirmed
# record replaces it.
GRANT_CARD_DAYS = 7


def draft_grant(records, gid):
    for r in records:
        if r.get("id") == gid:
            if r.get("kind") != "grant":
                raise Refused(f"{gid!r} is a {r.get('kind')} record, not a grant")
            if r.get("state") != "draft":
                raise Refused(f"grant {gid!r} is {r.get('state')}, not a draft; only a draft is confirmed on a card")
            if r["replaced_by"]:
                raise Refused(f"grant {gid!r} is already replaced by {', '.join(map(str, r['replaced_by']))}")
            return r
    raise Refused(f"no grant {gid!r} in the rulings file")


def cmd_grant_card(a):
    path = rulings_path()
    need_file(path)
    records, _, _ = fold_records(path)
    g = draft_grant(records, a.id)
    until = (parse_time(now()) + datetime.timedelta(days=GRANT_CARD_DAYS)).strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
    expires = g.get("expires") or "no expiry"
    card = f"""Source: {g.get('source', 'none recorded')} (draft grant {g['id']} in rulings.jsonl)

## Card 1. Confirm this grant: {g.get('subject', '')}?

**IN SHORT.** Director drafted a grant from your words. It has no effect until you confirm it here, and the bounds are listed below so you can check them.

**Problem.** Acting inside a grant is not an ask, so a grant has to show its limits before it counts. Draft {g['id']} is waiting for your answer.

**Terms.** Subject: {g.get('subject', '')}. Scope: {g.get('scope', '')}. To: {g.get('to', '')}. Expires: {expires}. Your words as recorded: {g.get('text', '')}

**Options.**
1. *Confirm it.* The grant counts from your answer, inside exactly the bounds above. The cost is that director acts within them without asking, one line per use in the digest.
2. *Do not confirm.* The draft stays a draft and director asks for each action. The cost is one ask per action.

**Recommendation.** Option 1, if the bounds match what you said.

**Valid until** {until}. Director re-checks it then.
"""
    if a.out:
        with open(a.out, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            f.write(card)
        print(f"dws: wrote the card for grant {g['id']} to {a.out}")
    else:
        sys.stdout.write(card)


def cmd_grant_confirm(a):
    if a.actor != "director":
        raise Refused(f"actor {a.actor!r} may not confirm a grant; only director does")
    quote = nonblank("quote", a.quote)
    card = record_id("card", a.card)
    path = rulings_path()
    need_file(path)
    snap, why = desk_snapshot()
    if snap is None:
        raise Refused(f"the Desk snapshot is {why}; a session reads the Desk and runs desk-snapshot write --answers")
    if "answered" not in snap:
        raise Refused("the Desk snapshot is UNREAD for answers: it was written without --answers")
    if not isinstance(snap["answered"], list) or not all(isinstance(x, str) for x in snap["answered"]):
        raise Refused("the Desk snapshot is UNREAD for answers: its answered field is not a list of card ids")
    if card not in snap["answered"]:
        raise Refused(f"card {card!r} is not answered in the Desk snapshot read at {snap['read_at']}; "
                      "a draft grant has no effect until the operator answers its card")
    with Locked(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(path) or ".", "rulings.lock")):
        records, _, _ = fold_records(path)
        g = draft_grant(records, a.id)
        taken = {r.get("id") for r in records}
        rid, n = f"{g['id']}-confirmed", 1
        while rid in taken:
            n += 1
            rid = f"{g['id']}-confirmed-{n}"
        rec = {"kind": "grant", "id": rid, "ts": now(), "actor": a.actor, "tag": "mirror",
               "source": stored_form(f"Desk card {card}, answered per the snapshot read {snap['read_at']}; "
                                     "the quote is the session's claim of the operator's words, not read by dws"),
               "subject": g["subject"], "scope": g["scope"], "to": g["to"], "state": "confirmed",
               "text": g["text"], "card": card, "quote": quote, "replaces": g["id"]}
        if g.get("expires"):
            rec["expires"] = g["expires"]
        append(rec, path)
    print(f"dws: wrote grant {rid}, confirmed on card {card}, replacing {a.id}; the quote is the session's claim, not read by dws")


# K11: the reconciler. It reads the Desk snapshot, the ledger, rulings.jsonl,
# rings.jsonl and the PR state the ledger observed, and writes proposals to a
# file of their own. It never appends a record to any store; director applies or
# drops each proposal (section 4 of the redesign, SOUL section 8). Every source
# prints its last-read time or UNREAD, a queue count reads "at least n" while any
# source is UNREAD, and a check whose source does not exist is listed as not run,
# never read as zero.
#
# Operator-editable, diagnostic only (ADR-007): a row not yet merged whose last
# move is older than this many days is close-or-kill input. A provisional value;
# the design leaves the idea threshold open (section 7).
UNMOVED_DAYS = {"default": 14, "idea": 14}
UNMOVED_STAGES = ("idea", "defined", "designed", "building", "in review")
# Checks that have no store a script can read yet. They are named in every run.
NOT_RUN_ALWAYS = (
    ("recommendation-sell-by", "no store of recommendations yet"),
    ("ask-unacked", "the ask ledger is the bus's (askledger.go); a script cannot read it yet"),
    ("harvest-due", "no harvest register a script can read yet (R-179)"),
)
DESK_CHECKS = ("blocked-no-open-card", "card-pr-merged", "duplicate-open-cards")


def reconcile_proposals_path():
    return os.path.join(STATE, "reconcile-proposals.json")


def reconcile_report():
    """The reconciler's report and the ledger's torn count, built from the stores and written nowhere.
    cmd_reconcile writes the proposals file; the digest reads the report and writes only digest.md."""
    t_now = now()
    when = parse_time(t_now)
    sources, not_run, proposals = {}, [], []

    snap, why = desk_snapshot()
    if snap is None:
        sources["desk"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": why}
    else:
        sources["desk"] = {"state": "read", "read_at": snap["read_at"]}
    desk_open = set(snap["open"]) if snap else None

    rows, torn = ({}, 0)
    if os.path.isfile(LEDGER):
        try:
            rows, torn = fold()
            if not rows and (torn or ledger_has_lines()):
                sources["ledger"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"{LEDGER} has no readable row (torn {torn})"}
            else:
                sources["ledger"] = {"state": "read", "read_at": t_now, "torn": torn}
        except OSError as err:
            sources["ledger"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"{LEDGER} cannot be read ({type(err).__name__})"}
    else:
        sources["ledger"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"no ledger at {LEDGER}"}
    ledger_ok = sources["ledger"]["state"] == "read"

    path = rulings_path()
    records = []
    if os.path.isfile(path):
        try:
            records, rtorn, _ = fold_records(path)
            if rtorn and not records:
                sources["rulings"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"{path} has no readable record (torn {rtorn})"}
            else:
                sources["rulings"] = {"state": "read", "read_at": t_now, "torn": rtorn}
        except OSError as err:
            sources["rulings"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"{path} cannot be read ({type(err).__name__})"}
    else:
        sources["rulings"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"no rulings file at {path}"}

    if os.path.isfile(RINGS):
        try:
            rseats, rtorn2 = fold_rings()
            if rtorn2 and not rseats:
                sources["rings"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"{RINGS} has no readable line (torn {rtorn2})"}
            else:
                sources["rings"] = {"state": "read", "read_at": t_now, "torn": rtorn2}
        except OSError as err:
            sources["rings"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"{RINGS} cannot be read ({type(err).__name__})"}
    else:
        sources["rings"] = {"state": "UNREAD", "why": f"no rings file at {RINGS}; no ring has been recorded"}

    checked = [o.get("checked_at") for row in rows.values() for link, o in row["observed"].items()
               if link.startswith("pr:") and isinstance(o, dict)]
    checked = sorted(c for c in checked if parse_ts(c))
    sources["prs"] = ({"state": "read", "read_at": checked[-1], "from": "PR observations in the ledger"} if checked
                      else {"state": "UNREAD", "why": "the ledger holds no PR observation; run dws refresh"})

    def merged(row):
        return [l for l, o in row["observed"].items()
                if l.startswith("pr:") and (o.get("seen") or {}).get("state") == "merged"]

    if ledger_ok and desk_open is not None:
        for slug, row in sorted(rows.items()):
            cards = [l[4:] for l in row["links"] if ASK.match(l)]
            open_cards = [c for c in cards if c in desk_open]
            if operator_blocked(row["blocked"]) and not open_cards and row["stage"] != "parked":
                proposals.append({"kind": "blocked-no-open-card", "subject": slug,
                                  "why": "blocked on the operator and no linked ask is open on the Desk",
                                  "evidence": {"links": row["links"], "desk_read_at": snap["read_at"]}})
            if open_cards and merged(row):
                proposals.append({"kind": "card-pr-merged", "subject": slug,
                                  "why": "a linked PR merged and the card is still open; director checks the result and closes it (Q5)",
                                  "evidence": {"cards": open_cards, "prs": merged(row)}})
            if len(open_cards) > 1:
                proposals.append({"kind": "duplicate-open-cards", "subject": slug,
                                  "why": "two open cards on one workstream",
                                  "evidence": {"cards": open_cards}})
    else:
        for c in DESK_CHECKS:
            not_run.append({"check": c, "why": "the " + ("Desk" if desk_open is None else "ledger") + " source is UNREAD"})

    if ledger_ok:
        for slug, row in sorted(rows.items()):
            if row["stage"] not in UNMOVED_STAGES:
                continue
            moved = parse_ts(row["last_moved"])
            days = UNMOVED_DAYS.get(row["stage"], UNMOVED_DAYS["default"])
            if moved and (when - moved).days >= days:
                proposals.append({"kind": "unmoved", "subject": slug,
                                  "why": f"not moved for {(when - moved).days} days (threshold {days}); close-or-kill input",
                                  "evidence": {"stage": row["stage"], "last_moved": row["last_moved"]}})
    else:
        not_run.append({"check": "unmoved", "why": "the ledger is UNREAD"})

    if sources["rulings"]["state"] == "read":
        for r in records:
            exp = r.get("expires")
            if r.get("kind") != "grant" or not isinstance(exp, str) or r["replaced_by"]:
                continue
            try:
                end = datetime.datetime.strptime(exp, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ" if "T" in exp else "%Y-%m-%d").replace(tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)
                if "T" not in exp:
                    # A date-only expiry holds through the end of that day.
                    end += datetime.timedelta(days=1)
            except ValueError:
                not_run.append({"check": f"grant-expired:{r.get('id')}", "why": f"the expiry {exp!r} does not parse (YYYY-MM-DD or YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ)"})
                continue
            if end < when:
                proposals.append({"kind": "grant-expired", "subject": str(r.get("id")),
                                  "why": f"grant expired {exp}; confirm a renewal or let it lapse",
                                  "evidence": {"state": r.get("state"), "scope": r.get("scope"), "expires": exp}})
    else:
        not_run.append({"check": "grant-expired", "why": "the rulings file is UNREAD"})

    for check, why in NOT_RUN_ALWAYS:
        not_run.append({"check": check, "why": why})
    for p in proposals:
        p["tag"] = "proposal"
        p["id"] = f"{p['kind']}:{p['subject']}"

    unread = sorted(k for k, v in sources.items() if v["state"] == "UNREAD")
    queue = {"count": len(desk_open) if desk_open is not None else None, "at_least": bool(unread)}
    report = {"read_at": t_now, "sources": sources, "queue": queue, "proposals": proposals, "not_run": not_run}
    return report, torn


def cmd_reconcile(a):
    report, torn = reconcile_report()
    sources, queue, proposals, not_run = report["sources"], report["queue"], report["proposals"], report["not_run"]

    out = a.out or reconcile_proposals_path()
    tmp = f"{out}.{os.getpid()}.tmp"
    try:
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(out)), exist_ok=True)
        with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            json.dump(report, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)
            f.write("\n")
            f.flush()
            os.fsync(f.fileno())
        os.replace(tmp, out)
    except OSError as err:
        try:
            os.unlink(tmp)
        except OSError:
            pass
        raise Refused(f"cannot write the proposals file {out} ({type(err).__name__}: {err.strerror or err}); "
                      "the report was not written. Name another file with --out")

    if a.json:
        json.dump(report, sys.stdout, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)
        print()
        return
    for name in ("desk", "ledger", "rulings", "rings", "prs"):
        v = sources[name]
        torn_note = f" (torn {v['torn']})" if v.get("torn") else ""
        print(f"{name:<8} " + (f"read {v['read_at']}{torn_note}" if v["state"] == "read" else f"UNREAD  {v['why']}"))
    if queue["count"] is None:
        print("queue    UNREAD (the Desk is not read)")
    else:
        print(f"queue    {'at least ' if queue['at_least'] else ''}{queue['count']} open card(s)")
    for p in proposals:
        print(f"propose  {p['id']}  {p['why']}")
    for n in not_run:
        print(f"not run  {n['check']}  {n['why']}")
    print(f"proposals written to {out}; no record was written")
    if torn:
        print(f"dws: {torn} unreadable line(s) in {LEDGER} skipped, not repaired", file=sys.stderr)


# D1: seat decisions (sim/design/seat-decisions.md, section 3). A decision is a run of
# events in workstreams.jsonl with "event": "decision" and an "op": add, then actual,
# confirm, override or rework. They are folded beside the rows under the same lock, so
# D2's wait edges can be checked against the decisions in one fold. director writes
# every event from the seat's seat-decision@1 message; the seat stays the author of the
# content. No move happens on a clock: a skip is no command, and the state stays.
DECISION_FORMAT = "seat-decision@1"
DECISION_FIELDS = ("id", "seat", "question", "options", "chosen", "test", "estimate", "undo", "changes")
# <seat label>-<YYYYMMDD>-<n>, lower case. A seat label may carry a team prefix (team-a/builder).
DECISION_ID = re.compile(r"^([a-z0-9][a-z0-9._/-]*)-([0-9]{8})-([0-9]+)$")
# card 1: the eight-line test, each line ok; a failed line sends the choice to the Desk
DECISION_TEST = re.compile(r"^" + r"[ ,;]+".join(f"{n} ok" for n in range(1, 9)) + r"$")
# card 2: at most 4 seat-hours in total, dependent work included
DECISION_ESTIMATE_MAX = 4
HOURS = re.compile(r"^([0-9]+(?:\.[0-9]+)?) ?h?$")
# The only moves (section 3): op -> (from, to). Anything else is no move, on write or on read.
DECISION_MOVES = {"confirm": ("decided-by-seat", "confirmed"),
                  "override": ("decided-by-seat", "overridden"),
                  "rework": ("overridden", "reworked")}
# card 1: a two-week trial; its start is given to --daily, never held in the ledger
TRIAL_DAYS = 14
# D2. The states a decision waits for the operator in: a seat decision, and a record of two paths.
DECISION_OPEN = ("decided-by-seat", "paths-open")
# card 4: at most three dependents for one decision, and none may start more than five days after it
WINDOW_DEPENDENTS = 3
WINDOW_HOURS = 120
WINDOW_FULL = "window full: stop, and the decision goes to the top of the operator's list"


def apply_decision(decisions, e):
    """One decision event into the decisions dict. An add for an id already held
    and a move from the wrong state are not applied: add refuses both on write,
    and a hand-written line cannot make a move the table does not have."""
    op, did, ts = e.get("op"), e.get("id"), e.get("ts", "")
    if op == "add":
        if not isinstance(did, str) or did in decisions:
            return
        decisions[did] = {"id": did, **{k: e.get(k) for k in ("seat", "question", "options", "chosen", "reason",
                                                             "test", "estimate_h", "undo")},
                          "changes": list(e.get("changes", [])), "actual_h": None, "actual_source": None,
                          "state": "decided-by-seat", "added": ts, "moves": []}
        return
    if op == "paths":
        # D2 section 8: one record for two paths, open until pick or withdraw
        if not isinstance(did, str) or did in decisions:
            return
        a, b = e.get("a") or {}, e.get("b") or {}
        m = DECISION_ID.match(did)
        decisions[did] = {"id": did, "seat": m.group(1) if m else "", "question": f"which path for card {e.get('card')}",
                          "options": f"a: {a.get('row')}; b: {b.get('row')}", "chosen": None, "reason": None,
                          "test": a.get("test"), "estimate_h": (a.get("estimate") or 0) + (b.get("estimate") or 0),
                          "undo": None, "changes": [], "actual_h": None, "actual_source": None,
                          "state": "paths-open", "added": ts, "moves": [],
                          "paths": {"card": e.get("card"), "evidence": e.get("evidence"),
                                    "why_waiting": e.get("why_waiting"), "a": a, "b": b}}
        return
    d = decisions.get(did)
    if d is None:
        return
    if op == "pick" and d["state"] == "paths-open" and e.get("winner") in ("a", "b"):
        w = d["paths"][e["winner"]]
        d["chosen"], d["estimate_h"], d["state"] = f"path {e['winner']}: {w.get('row')}", w.get("estimate"), "decided-by-seat"
        d["moves"].append({"to": d["state"], "ts": ts, "op": "pick", "winner": e["winner"], "result": e.get("result")})
        return
    if op == "withdraw" and d["state"] == "paths-open":
        d["state"] = "withdrawn"
        d["moves"].append({"to": d["state"], "ts": ts, **{k: e[k] for k in ("words", "ref") if k in e}})
        return
    if op == "actual":
        d["actual_h"], d["actual_source"] = e.get("hours"), e.get("source")
    elif op in DECISION_MOVES and d["state"] == DECISION_MOVES[op][0]:
        d["state"] = DECISION_MOVES[op][1]
        d["moves"].append({"to": d["state"], "ts": ts,
                           **{k: e[k] for k in ("words", "ref", "instead") if k in e}})


def decision_block(text):
    """The fields of one seat-decision@1 block, or Refused. A leading line naming the
    format is allowed; every other non-blank line is 'field: value', each field once."""
    lines = [l for l in text.splitlines() if l.strip()]
    if lines and lines[0].strip() == DECISION_FORMAT:
        lines = lines[1:]
    fields = {}
    for line in lines:
        key, sep, value = line.partition(":")
        key = key.strip()
        if not sep or not key:
            raise Refused(f"line {line.strip()!r} is not a 'field: value' line of {DECISION_FORMAT}")
        if key not in DECISION_FIELDS:
            raise Refused(f"unknown field {key!r}; {DECISION_FORMAT} fields are {', '.join(DECISION_FIELDS)}")
        if key in fields:
            raise Refused(f"field {key!r} is repeated; each field is given once")
        fields[key] = value
    missing = [k for k in DECISION_FIELDS if not stored_form(fields.get(k, ""))]
    if missing:
        raise Refused(f"field(s) missing or empty: {', '.join(missing)}")
    return fields


def decision_event(fields):
    """The add event's fields from a parsed block, each through checked() so no
    instance id is stored; Refused when the id, test, estimate or chosen line is not
    in its form."""
    did = checked("id", fields["id"])
    if not DECISION_ID.match(did):
        raise Refused(f"id {did!r} is not <seat label>-<YYYYMMDD>-<n> in lower case")
    try:
        datetime.datetime.strptime(DECISION_ID.match(did).group(2), "%Y%m%d")
    except ValueError:
        raise Refused(f"id {did!r} does not carry a real date as YYYYMMDD")
    chosen, because, reason = checked("chosen", fields["chosen"]).partition(" because ")
    if not because or not chosen.strip() or not reason.strip():
        raise Refused("chosen has no ' because <reason>'; the line reads chosen: <option> because <reason>")
    test = checked("test", fields["test"])
    if not DECISION_TEST.match(test.lower()):
        raise Refused(f"test {test!r} does not read 1 ok to 8 ok; a decision that fails a line of the "
                      "eight-line test goes to the Desk, not the ledger")
    m = HOURS.match(checked("estimate", fields["estimate"]))
    if not m:
        raise Refused(f"estimate {fields['estimate'].strip()!r} is not a number of seat-hours")
    estimate = float(m.group(1))
    if estimate > DECISION_ESTIMATE_MAX:
        raise Refused(f"estimate {estimate:g}h is over {DECISION_ESTIMATE_MAX} seat-hours (card 2); "
                      "a larger choice goes to the Desk")
    changes = [decision_link(typed_link(checked("changes", x))) for x in stored_form(fields["changes"]).split(" ")]
    return {"event": "decision", "op": "add", "id": did, "seat": checked("seat", fields["seat"]),
            "question": checked("question", fields["question"]), "options": checked("options", fields["options"]),
            "chosen": chosen.strip(), "reason": reason.strip(), "test": test, "estimate_h": estimate,
            "undo": checked("undo", fields["undo"]), "changes": changes}


DECISION_LINK_KINDS = ("pr:", "issue:", "bd:", "relay:", "msg:")


def decision_link(link):
    """A changes entry is one of the typed link kinds, and one that starts with pr:,
    issue: or bd: must fully match LINK, so a comma list is not stored as one link.
    relay: and msg: keep typed_link's checks. ask: is left out: a Desk card is not a
    change. Row links (typed_link, dws link) are unchanged."""
    if not link.startswith(DECISION_LINK_KINDS):
        raise Refused(f"changes link {link!r} is not a typed link; give pr:, issue:, bd:, relay: or msg: "
                      "links, separated by spaces")
    if link.startswith(("pr:", "issue:", "bd:")) and not LINK.fullmatch(link):
        raise Refused(f"changes link {link!r} is not pr:<owner>/<repo>#<n>, issue:<owner>/<repo>#<n> "
                      "or bd:<id>; give each link once, separated by spaces")
    return link


def write_decision(actor, event, check):
    """Fold, check, append under the ledger lock, as write() does for rows;
    check(decisions) raises Refused."""
    event = stamp(actor, event)
    with Locked():
        decisions = {}
        fold(decisions=decisions)
        check(decisions)
        append(event)
    rerender()


def need_decision(decisions, did):
    if did not in decisions:
        raise Refused(f"no decision {did!r}; add it first with dws decision add --from FILE")
    return decisions[did]


def cmd_decision_add(a):
    try:
        with open(a.from_, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            text = f.read()
    except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError) as err:
        raise Refused(f"cannot read {a.from_} ({type(err).__name__}); nothing written")
    ev = decision_event(decision_block(text))

    def check(decisions):
        if ev["id"] in decisions:
            raise Refused(f"decision {ev['id']!r} is already in the ledger; nothing written")
    write_decision(a.actor, ev, check)
    print(f"dws: wrote decision {ev['id']} (decided-by-seat)")


def cmd_decision_actual(a):
    m = HOURS.match(stored_form(a.hours))
    if not m:
        raise Refused(f"--hours {a.hours!r} is not a number of seat-hours")
    ev = {"event": "decision", "op": "actual", "id": a.id, "hours": float(m.group(1)),
          "source": checked("source", nonblank("source", a.source))}
    write_decision(a.actor, ev, lambda decisions: need_decision(decisions, a.id))
    print(f"dws: recorded {float(m.group(1)):g}h actual for decision {a.id}")


def decision_move(a, op, extra=None):
    """confirm, override or rework: Refused unless the decision is in the move's from state."""
    frm, to = DECISION_MOVES[op]
    ev = {"event": "decision", "op": op, "id": a.id, **(extra or {})}
    held = {}

    def check(decisions):
        d = need_decision(decisions, a.id)
        if d["state"] != frm:
            why = "rework follows an override only" if op == "rework" else \
                "a confirm or override answers an unconfirmed decision only"
            raise Refused(f"decision {a.id!r} is {d['state']!r}, not {frm!r}; {why}")
        held.update(d)
    write_decision(a.actor, ev, check)
    print(f"dws: decision {a.id} {to}")
    return held


def operator_words(a):
    # The operator's words are stored as given, never normalized (R-150, R-186).
    return {"words": nonblank("words", a.words), "ref": stored_form(nonblank("ref", a.ref))}


def cmd_decision_confirm(a):
    decision_move(a, "confirm", operator_words(a))


def dependents(rows, did):
    """Card 4: the rows with an edge to the decision whose stage is not parked."""
    return [r for r in rows.values() if did in r.get("waits", []) and r["stage"] != "parked"]


def affected(rows, did):
    """Section 6: every row with an edge to the decision, with its stage and its pr: links."""
    return [{"slug": r["slug"], "stage": r["stage"], "prs": [l for l in r["links"] if l.startswith("pr:")]}
            for r in sorted(rows.values(), key=lambda r: r["slug"]) if did in r.get("waits", [])]


def window_check(rows, decisions, did, slug, t_now):
    """Section 5, checks 1 to 3, for a row that would be a dependent of the decision. Refused
    unless the decision is decided-by-seat, has fewer than three other dependents, and was added
    no more than 120 hours ago by the ledger clock."""
    if did not in decisions:
        raise Refused(f"no decision {did!r}; add it first with dws decision add --from FILE")
    d = decisions[did]
    if d["state"] != "decided-by-seat":
        raise Refused(f"decision {did!r} is {d['state']!r}, not 'decided-by-seat'; a confirmed decision needs no "
                      "window, and an overridden, withdrawn or paths-open one takes no new work")
    others = [r["slug"] for r in dependents(rows, did) if r["slug"] != slug]
    if len(others) >= WINDOW_DEPENDENTS:
        raise Refused(f"decision {did!r} already has {len(others)} dependents ({', '.join(sorted(others))}); {WINDOW_FULL}")
    added = parse_ts(d.get("added"))
    if added is not None and (t_now - added).total_seconds() > WINDOW_HOURS * 3600:
        hours = int((t_now - added).total_seconds() // 3600)
        raise Refused(f"decision {did!r} was decided {hours} hours ago, past the {WINDOW_HOURS}-hour window; {WINDOW_FULL}")


def print_affected(rows, did):
    print("rows that wait on it:")
    for x in affected(rows, did):
        print(f"  {x['slug']}  {x['stage']}  {' '.join(x['prs'])}".rstrip())
    if not affected(rows, did):
        print("  none")


def cmd_decision_override(a):
    d = decision_move(a, "override", {**operator_words(a), "instead": stored_form(nonblank("instead", a.instead))})
    print("the decision's own changes:")
    for link in d["changes"]:
        print(f"  {link}")
    rows, _ = fold()
    print_affected(rows, a.id)


def cmd_decision_rework(a):
    """Section 6: refused while any row with an edge to the decision is not parked."""
    def plan(rows, decisions):
        d = need_decision(decisions, a.id)
        if d["state"] != "overridden":
            raise Refused(f"decision {a.id!r} is {d['state']!r}, not 'overridden'; rework follows an override only")
        open_ = [r["slug"] for r in dependents(rows, a.id)]
        if open_:
            raise Refused(f"decision {a.id!r} still has {len(open_)} affected row(s) that are not closed or redone: "
                          f"{', '.join(sorted(open_))}; park a row whose work was closed, or --unwait one redone on the new choice")
        return [{"event": "decision", "op": "rework", "id": a.id}]
    write_plan(a.actor, plan)
    print(f"dws: decision {a.id} reworked")


def paths_hours(flag, value):
    m = HOURS.match(stored_form(value))
    if not m:
        raise Refused(f"{flag} {value!r} is not a number of seat-hours")
    return float(m.group(1))


def paths_test(flag, value):
    if not DECISION_TEST.match(stored_form(value).lower()):
        raise Refused(f"{flag} {value!r} does not read 1 ok to 8 ok; all four parts must hold (card 6, part 4: eight oks)")
    return stored_form(value)


def cmd_decision_paths(a):
    """Section 8: two paths at once for a card that waits on the operator, as one record."""
    did = checked("id", stored_form(a.id))
    if not DECISION_ID.match(did):
        raise Refused(f"id {did!r} must be <seat label>-<YYYYMMDD>-<n>, lower case")
    est_a, est_b = paths_hours("--estimate-a", a.estimate_a), paths_hours("--estimate-b", a.estimate_b)
    if est_a + est_b > DECISION_ESTIMATE_MAX:
        raise Refused(f"the two estimates add to {est_a + est_b:g} seat-hours, over {DECISION_ESTIMATE_MAX} (card 6, part 1)")
    test_a, test_b = paths_test("--test-a", a.test_a), paths_test("--test-b", a.test_b)
    evidence = checked("evidence", nonblank("evidence", a.evidence))
    why = checked("why-waiting", nonblank("why-waiting", a.why_waiting))
    row_a, row_b = stored_form(a.row_a), stored_form(a.row_b)
    if row_a == row_b:
        raise Refused("the two rows must be two rows: --row-a and --row-b name the same workstream")
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]*", a.card):
        raise Refused(f"--card {a.card!r} is not a card id")
    print(f"dws: {desk_card_open(a.card)}")
    ev = {"event": "decision", "op": "paths", "id": did, "card": a.card, "evidence": evidence, "why_waiting": why,
          "a": {"row": row_a, "estimate": est_a, "test": test_a}, "b": {"row": row_b, "estimate": est_b, "test": test_b}}

    def plan(rows, decisions):
        if did in decisions:
            raise Refused(f"decision {did!r} is already in the ledger; nothing written")
        for x in decisions.values():
            if x.get("paths", {}).get("card") == a.card:
                raise Refused(f"card {a.card!r} already has a paths record ({x['id']!r}, {x['state']}); one card gets one pair "
                              "of paths, ever. A reworked and reposted card has a new id, and may get a new pair")
        need(rows, row_a), need(rows, row_b)
        return [ev, {"event": "wait", "ws": row_a, "add": [did]}, {"event": "wait", "ws": row_b, "add": [did]}]
    write_plan(a.actor, plan)
    print(f"dws: wrote paths record {did} (paths-open); edges set on {row_a} and {row_b}")


def cmd_decision_pick(a):
    if a.winner not in ("a", "b"):
        raise Refused(f"--winner is a or b, not {a.winner!r}")
    result = checked("result", nonblank("result", a.result))

    def plan(rows, decisions):
        d = need_decision(decisions, a.id)
        if d["state"] != "paths-open":
            raise Refused(f"decision {a.id!r} is {d['state']!r}, not 'paths-open'; pick records the evidence for a paths record only")
        loser = d["paths"]["b" if a.winner == "a" else "a"]["row"]
        stage = rows[loser]["stage"] if loser in rows else None
        if stage != "parked":
            raise Refused(f"the losing path's row {loser!r} is {stage!r}, not 'parked'; park it, and close its PR as a draft, first")
        return [{"event": "decision", "op": "pick", "id": a.id, "winner": a.winner, "result": result}]
    write_plan(a.actor, plan)
    print(f"dws: decision {a.id} decided-by-seat (path {a.winner}); the operator still confirms it")


def cmd_decision_withdraw(a):
    words = {"words": nonblank("words", a.words), "ref": stored_form(nonblank("ref", a.ref))}

    def plan(rows, decisions):
        d = need_decision(decisions, a.id)
        if d["state"] != "paths-open":
            raise Refused(f"decision {a.id!r} is {d['state']!r}, not 'paths-open'; withdraw ends a paths record only")
        live = [d["paths"][k]["row"] for k in ("a", "b") if rows.get(d["paths"][k]["row"], {}).get("stage") != "parked"]
        if live:
            raise Refused(f"row(s) {', '.join(live)} are not parked; park both paths before the record is withdrawn")
        return [{"event": "decision", "op": "withdraw", "id": a.id, **words}]
    write_plan(a.actor, plan)
    print(f"dws: decision {a.id} withdrawn")


def cmd_merge_hold(a):
    """The read merge-guard makes (section 5): Refused, with the line merge-guard prints, when a row
    that links the PR waits on a decision that is not confirmed. A PR no row links is not held."""
    m = re.fullmatch(r"([^#\s]+)#([0-9]+)", a.pr)
    if not m:
        raise Refused(f"{a.pr!r} is not <owner/repo>#<number>")
    want = f"pr:{m.group(1).lower()}#{m.group(2)}"
    decisions = {}
    try:
        rows, torn = fold(decisions=decisions)
    except OSError as err:
        print(f"dws: the ledger cannot be read ({type(err).__name__})", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)
    if torn:
        # A torn line may be the wait event that holds this PR; skipping it would let the PR through.
        print(f"dws: {torn} unreadable line(s) in {LEDGER}; cannot tell whether a row waits on {a.pr}, so the merge is held", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)
    held = []
    for r in sorted(rows.values(), key=lambda r: r["slug"]):
        if want not in [l.lower() for l in r["links"] if l.startswith("pr:")]:
            continue
        for did in r.get("waits", []):
            if decisions.get(did, {}).get("state") != "confirmed":
                held.append(f"waits on seat decision {did}, not confirmed (seat-decide-window)")
    if held:
        raise Refused("; ".join(dict.fromkeys(held)))


def decision_at_risk(d):
    """The seat-hours an override would throw away: actual_h where recorded, else estimate_h."""
    h = d.get("actual_h") if d.get("actual_h") is not None else d.get("estimate_h")
    return h if isinstance(h, (int, float)) else 0


def decision_view(d, t_now, rows):
    added = parse_ts(d.get("added"))
    age = max(0, int((t_now - added).total_seconds() // 86400)) if added else None
    waiting = len(dependents(rows, d["id"]))
    past = added is not None and (t_now - added).total_seconds() > WINDOW_HOURS * 3600
    full = d["state"] == "decided-by-seat" and (waiting >= WINDOW_DEPENDENTS or (past and waiting >= 1))
    return {**d, "age_days": age, "waiting": waiting, "window_full": full, "at_risk_h": decision_at_risk(d),
            "affected": affected(rows, d["id"])}


def decision_order(v):
    """Card 4's order for the unconfirmed: a full window first, then most dependents, then oldest,
    then most seat-hours at risk; ties by seat label, date, then <n> as a number."""
    m = DECISION_ID.match(v["id"])
    tie = (m.group(1), m.group(2), int(m.group(3))) if m else (v["id"], "", 0)
    return (0 if v["window_full"] else 1, -v["waiting"], v.get("added") or "", -v["at_risk_h"]) + tie


def cmd_decisions(a):
    decisions = {}
    rows, torn = fold(decisions=decisions)
    t_now = parse_time(now())
    views = [decision_view(d, t_now, rows) for d in decisions.values()]
    open_ = sorted((v for v in views if v["state"] in DECISION_OPEN), key=decision_order)
    rest = sorted((v for v in views if v["state"] not in DECISION_OPEN), key=lambda v: (v.get("added") or "", v["id"]))
    listed = open_ if a.unconfirmed else open_ + rest
    if a.daily:
        today = t_now.date()
        if a.trial_start is None:
            day = "trial day unknown (no --trial-start)"
        else:
            try:
                start = datetime.datetime.strptime(a.trial_start, "%Y-%m-%d").date()
                day = f"trial day {(today - start).days + 1} of {TRIAL_DAYS}"
            except ValueError:
                day = f"trial day unknown (--trial-start {a.trial_start!r} is not YYYY-MM-DD)"
        new = sum(1 for v in views if (v.get("added") or "")[:10] == today.isoformat())
        confirmed = sum(1 for v in views if v["state"] == "confirmed")
        overridden = [v for v in views if v["state"] in ("overridden", "reworked")]
        rework = sum(v["at_risk_h"] for v in overridden)
        print(f"Seat decisions ({day}): {new} new today, {len(views)} total, {confirmed} confirmed, "
              f"{len(overridden)} overridden, rework {rework:g} seat-hours.")
        print("Unconfirmed, most work held first:")
        for v in open_:
            print(f"  {v['id']}  {v['waiting']} waiting, {v['age_days']}d old, {v['at_risk_h']:g}h at risk: {v['question']}")
        if not open_:
            print("  none")
    elif a.json:
        json.dump({"ledger": LEDGER, "torn": torn, "decisions": listed}, sys.stdout, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)
        print()
    else:
        cols = ("state", "decision", "seat", "age", "estimate", "actual", "question")
        table = [cols] + [(v["state"], v["id"], v["seat"], f"{v['age_days']}d", f"{v['estimate_h']:g}h",
                           "" if v["actual_h"] is None else f"{v['actual_h']:g}h", v["question"]) for v in listed]
        widths = [max(len(str(row[i])) for row in table) for i in range(len(cols))]
        for row in table:
            print("  ".join(str(c).ljust(w) for c, w in zip(row, widths)).rstrip())
    if torn:
        print(f"dws: {torn} unreadable line(s) in {LEDGER} skipped, not repaired", file=sys.stderr)


# W3: `page` renders the ledger as one self-contained HTML page, from workstreams.jsonl and
# desk-snapshot.json. No network, no external script, no clock in the output: the same inputs
# and the same DWS_NOW give the same bytes. The look and the nav are instance files, never
# repo content: --theme and --nav (defaults page-theme.css.html and page-nav.html in the
# state directory) are put verbatim at the top of the body, and with neither the page falls
# back to a plain built-in style and no nav. The "Your call" control on a row writes a doc
# to the page's db; `picks` reads an export of those docs back (below).
#
# A row lands in at most one section, first match wins:
#   blocked on the operator (open stage)          Blocked on you, ad hoc or not
#   slug starts adhoc-                            Ad hoc, whatever its stage or seat block; a parked
#                                                 or finished one leaves 7 days after it last moved
#   merged, released, deployed, accepted, 7 days  Done in the last 7 days
#   blocked on anything else, open stage          Waiting on a seat (a seat or a role)
#   any other open stage, moved under 7 days ago  In motion (idea, defined, designed, building,
#                                                 in review)
#   any other open stage, moved 7 days ago or more  Quiet 7 days or more
# Every row with an open stage lands in exactly one section. Only a row that is parked, or
# finished more than 7 days ago, is counted in the footer instead.
# A blocked value of "none" or nothing is not blocked, as `dws set` writes it. A row in none
# of the sections is counted in the footer, never dropped without a word.
# The 7 days and the lists are the operator's to change here.
PAGE_TITLE = "Director: Work Ledger"
PAGE_ID = "work-ledger"
PAGE_DAYS = 7
DONE_STAGES = ("merged", "released", "deployed", "accepted")
CLOSED_STAGES = DONE_STAGES + ("parked",)
# (key, heading, the one line under it, the calls a row in it may carry as (action, label))
PAGE_SECTIONS = (
    ("blocked", "Blocked on you", "Waiting on your answer; each row names its Desk card, or says none is linked.", ()),
    ("motion", "In motion", f"Open work moved in the last {PAGE_DAYS} days.",
     (("nudge-owner", "Nudge owner"), ("mark-done", "Mark done"))),
    ("waiting", "Waiting on a seat", "Blocked on a seat or a role, not on you.",
     (("nudge-owner", "Nudge owner"), ("reassign", "Reassign"), ("park", "Park"))),
    ("adhoc", "Ad hoc", f"Ad hoc streams: open ones always, parked or finished ones for {PAGE_DAYS} days after they last moved.",
     (("nudge-owner", "Nudge owner"), ("close", "Close"), ("park", "Park"))),
    ("done", f"Done in the last {PAGE_DAYS} days", f"Merged, released, deployed or accepted in the last {PAGE_DAYS} days.", ()),
    ("quiet", f"Quiet {PAGE_DAYS} days or more", f"Open work not moved for {PAGE_DAYS} days or more.",
     (("kick-off", "Kick off"), ("park", "Park"), ("close", "Close"))),
)
# Sections listed oldest move first; the others newest first.
PAGE_OLDEST_FIRST = ("blocked", "waiting", "quiet")

PAGE_CSS = """
